// The Jesus Bible -- Mark, Romans, Galatians, Ephesians, Philippians, Colossians, and Titus so far, recast into the voice of Jesus.
// KJV wording preserved; see VoiceOfJesus/STATUS.md for the method and rules.
const JESUS_BOOKS = [{"name":"Mark","order":1,"testament":"NT","chapters":16},{"name":"Romans","order":2,"testament":"NT","chapters":16},{"name":"Galatians","order":3,"testament":"NT","chapters":6},{"name":"Ephesians","order":4,"testament":"NT","chapters":6},{"name":"Philippians","order":5,"testament":"NT","chapters":4},{"name":"Colossians","order":6,"testament":"NT","chapters":4},{"name":"Titus","order":7,"testament":"NT","chapters":3}];
const JESUS = [{"ref":"Mark 1","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"The Beginning of the Good News","verses":[["1:1","The beginning of the gospel: I am Jesus Christ, the Son of God;"],["1:2","As it is written in the prophets, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face, which shall prepare thy way before thee."],["1:3","The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make his paths straight."]]},{"heading":"John in the Wilderness","verses":[["1:4","John did baptize in the wilderness, and preach the baptism of repentance for the remission of sins."],["1:5","And there went out unto him all the land of Judea, and they of Jerusalem, and were all baptized of him in the river of Jordan, confessing their sins."],["1:6","And John was clothed with camel's hair, and with a girdle of a skin about his loins; and he did eat locusts and wild honey;"]]},{"heading":"Water and the Spirit","verses":[["1:7","And preached, saying, There cometh one mightier than I after me, the latchet of whose shoes I am not worthy to stoop down and unloose."],["1:8","I indeed have baptized you with water: but he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost."]]},{"heading":"The Voice from Heaven","verses":[["1:9","And it came to pass in those days, that I came from Nazareth of Galilee, and was baptized of John in Jordan."],["1:10","And straightway coming up out of the water, I saw the heavens opened, and the Spirit like a dove descending upon me:"],["1:11","And there came a voice from heaven, saying, Thou art my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased."]]},{"heading":"Forty Days in the Wilderness","verses":[["1:12","And immediately the Spirit driveth me into the wilderness."],["1:13","And I was there in the wilderness forty days, tempted of Satan; and was with the wild beasts; and the angels ministered unto me."]]},{"heading":"The Time Has Come","verses":[["1:14","Now after that John was put in prison, I came into Galilee, preaching the gospel of the kingdom of God,"],["1:15","And saying, The time is fulfilled, and the kingdom of God is at hand: repent ye, and believe the gospel."]]},{"heading":"Four Fishermen by the Sea","verses":[["1:16","Now as I walked by the sea of Galilee, I saw Simon and Andrew his brother casting a net into the sea: for they were fishers."],["1:17","And I said unto them, Come ye after me, and I will make you to become fishers of men."],["1:18","And straightway they forsook their nets, and followed me."],["1:19","And when I had gone a little further thence, I saw James the son of Zebedee, and John his brother, who also were in the ship mending their nets."],["1:20","And straightway I called them: and they left their father Zebedee in the ship with the hired servants, and went after me."]]},{"heading":"An Authority All His Own","verses":[["1:21","And they went into Capernaum; and straightway on the sabbath day I entered into the synagogue, and taught."],["1:22","And they were astonished at my doctrine: for I taught them as one that had authority, and not as the scribes."]]},{"heading":"The Unclean Spirit Cries Out","verses":[["1:23","And there was in their synagogue a man with an unclean spirit; and he cried out,"],["1:24","Saying, Let us alone; what have we to do with thee, thou Jesus of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us? I know thee who thou art, the Holy One of God."],["1:25","And I rebuked him, saying, Hold thy peace, and come out of him."],["1:26","And when the unclean spirit had torn him, and cried with a loud voice, he came out of him."],["1:27","And they were all amazed, insomuch that they questioned among themselves, saying, What thing is this? what new doctrine is this? for with authority commandeth he even the unclean spirits, and they do obey him."],["1:28","And immediately my fame spread abroad throughout all the region round about Galilee."]]},{"heading":"He Took Her by the Hand","verses":[["1:29","And forthwith, when we were come out of the synagogue, we entered into the house of Simon and Andrew, with James and John."],["1:30","But Simon's wife's mother lay sick of a fever, and anon they tell me of her."],["1:31","And I came and took her by the hand, and lifted her up; and immediately the fever left her, and she ministered unto us."]]},{"heading":"The Whole Town at the Door","verses":[["1:32","And at even, when the sun did set, they brought unto me all that were diseased, and them that were possessed with devils."],["1:33","And all the city was gathered together at the door."],["1:34","And I healed many that were sick of divers diseases, and cast out many devils; and suffered not the devils to speak, because they knew me."]]},{"heading":"Alone Before Daylight","verses":[["1:35","And in the morning, rising up a great while before day, I went out, and departed into a solitary place, and there prayed."],["1:36","And Simon and they that were with him followed after me."],["1:37","And when they had found me, they said unto me, All men seek for thee."],["1:38","And I said unto them, Let us go into the next towns, that I may preach there also: for therefore came I forth."],["1:39","And I preached in their synagogues throughout all Galilee, and cast out devils."]]},{"heading":"Moved with Compassion","verses":[["1:40","And there came a leper to me, beseeching me, and kneeling down to me, and saying unto me, If thou wilt, thou canst make me clean."],["1:41","And I, moved with compassion, put forth my hand, and touched him, and say unto him, I will; be thou clean."],["1:42","And as soon as I had spoken, immediately the leprosy departed from him, and he was cleansed."]]},{"heading":"He Could Not Stay Hidden","verses":[["1:43","And I straitly charged him, and forthwith sent him away;"],["1:44","And say unto him, See thou say nothing to any man: but go thy way, shew thyself to the priest, and offer for thy cleansing those things which Moses commanded, for a testimony unto them."],["1:45","But he went out, and began to publish it much, and to blaze abroad the matter, insomuch that I could no more openly enter into the city, but was without in desert places: and they came to me from every quarter."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 2","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"A Roof Torn Open","verses":[["2:1","And again I entered into Capernaum after some days; and it was noised that I was in the house."],["2:2","And straightway many were gathered together, insomuch that there was no room to receive them, no, not so much as about the door: and I preached the word unto them."],["2:3","And they come unto me, bringing one sick of the palsy, which was borne of four."],["2:4","And when they could not come nigh unto me for the press, they uncovered the roof where I was: and when they had broken it up, they let down the bed wherein the sick of the palsy lay."],["2:5","When I saw their faith, I said unto the sick of the palsy, Son, thy sins be forgiven thee."]]},{"heading":"Forgiven First, Then Healed","verses":[["2:6","But there were certain of the scribes sitting there, and reasoning in their hearts,"],["2:7","Why doth this man thus speak blasphemies? who can forgive sins but God only?"],["2:8","And immediately when I perceived in my spirit that they so reasoned within themselves, I said unto them, Why reason ye these things in your hearts?"],["2:9","Whether is it easier to say to the sick of the palsy, Thy sins be forgiven thee; or to say, Arise, and take up thy bed, and walk?"],["2:10","But that ye may know that I, the Son of man, have power on earth to forgive sins, (I say to the sick of the palsy,)"],["2:11","I say unto thee, Arise, and take up thy bed, and go thy way into thine house."],["2:12","And immediately he arose, took up the bed, and went forth before them all; insomuch that they were all amazed, and glorified God, saying, We never saw it on this fashion."]]},{"heading":"Levi at the Tax Booth","verses":[["2:13","And I went forth again by the sea side; and all the multitude resorted unto me, and I taught them."],["2:14","And as I passed by, I saw Levi the son of Alpheus sitting at the receipt of custom, and said unto him, Follow me. And he arose and followed me."]]},{"heading":"At the Table with Sinners","verses":[["2:15","And it came to pass, that, as I sat at meat in my house, many publicans and sinners sat also together with me and my disciples: for there were many, and they followed me."],["2:16","And when the scribes and Pharisees saw me eat with publicans and sinners, they said unto my disciples, How is it that he eateth and drinketh with publicans and sinners?"],["2:17","When I heard it, I say unto them, They that are whole have no need of the physician, but they that are sick: I came not to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance."]]},{"heading":"The Bridegroom Is Still Here","verses":[["2:18","And the disciples of John and of the Pharisees used to fast: and they come and say unto me, Why do the disciples of John and of the Pharisees fast, but thy disciples fast not?"],["2:19","And I said unto them, Can the children of the bridechamber fast, while the bridegroom is with them? as long as they have the bridegroom with them, they cannot fast."],["2:20","But the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken away from them, and then shall they fast in those days."]]},{"heading":"New Wine, New Skins","verses":[["2:21","No man also seweth a piece of new cloth on an old garment: else the new piece that filled it up taketh away from the old, and the rent is made worse."],["2:22","And no man putteth new wine into old bottles: else the new wine doth burst the bottles, and the wine is spilled, and the bottles will be marred: but new wine must be put into new bottles."]]},{"heading":"The Sabbath Was Made for People","verses":[["2:23","And it came to pass, that I went through the corn fields on the sabbath day; and my disciples began, as they went, to pluck the ears of corn."],["2:24","And the Pharisees said unto me, Behold, why do they on the sabbath day that which is not lawful?"],["2:25","And I said unto them, Have ye never read what David did, when he had need, and was an hungred, he, and they that were with him?"],["2:26","How he went into the house of God in the days of Abiathar the high priest, and did eat the shewbread, which is not lawful to eat but for the priests, and gave also to them which were with him?"],["2:27","And I said unto them, The sabbath was made for man, and not man for the sabbath:"],["2:28","Therefore I, the Son of man, am Lord also of the sabbath."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 3","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"A Hand Made Whole","verses":[["3:1","And I entered again into the synagogue; and there was a man there which had a withered hand."],["3:2","And they watched me, whether I would heal him on the sabbath day; that they might accuse me."],["3:3","And I say unto the man which had the withered hand, Stand forth."],["3:4","And I say unto them, Is it lawful to do good on the sabbath days, or to do evil? to save life, or to kill? But they held their peace."],["3:5","And when I had looked round about on them with anger, being grieved for the hardness of their hearts, I say unto the man, Stretch forth thine hand. And he stretched it out: and his hand was restored whole as the other."],["3:6","And the Pharisees went forth, and straightway took counsel with the Herodians against me, how they might destroy me."]]},{"heading":"Crowds from Every Direction","verses":[["3:7","But I withdrew myself with my disciples to the sea: and a great multitude from Galilee followed me, and from Judea,"],["3:8","And from Jerusalem, and from Idumea, and from beyond Jordan; and they about Tyre and Sidon, a great multitude, when they had heard what great things I did, came unto me."],["3:9","And I spake to my disciples, that a small ship should wait on me because of the multitude, lest they should throng me."],["3:10","For I had healed many; insomuch that they pressed upon me for to touch me, as many as had plagues."],["3:11","And unclean spirits, when they saw me, fell down before me, and cried, saying, Thou art the Son of God."],["3:12","And I straitly charged them that they should not make me known."]]},{"heading":"The Twelve He Chose","verses":[["3:13","And I go up into a mountain, and call unto me whom I would: and they came unto me."],["3:14","And I ordained twelve, that they should be with me, and that I might send them forth to preach,"],["3:15","And to have power to heal sicknesses, and to cast out devils:"],["3:16","And Simon I surnamed Peter;"],["3:17","And James the son of Zebedee, and John the brother of James; and I surnamed them Boanerges, which is, The sons of thunder:"],["3:18","And Andrew, and Philip, and Bartholomew, and Matthew, and Thomas, and James the son of Alpheus, and Thaddeus, and Simon the Canaanite,"],["3:19","And Judas Iscariot, which also betrayed me: and we went into an house."]]},{"heading":"No Time Even to Eat","verses":[["3:20","And the multitude cometh together again, so that we could not so much as eat bread."],["3:21","And when my friends heard of it, they went out to lay hold on me: for they said, He is beside himself."],["3:22","And the scribes which came down from Jerusalem said, He hath Beelzebub, and by the prince of the devils casteth he out devils."]]},{"heading":"A Kingdom Divided Cannot Stand","verses":[["3:23","And I called them unto me, and said unto them in parables, How can Satan cast out Satan?"],["3:24","And if a kingdom be divided against itself, that kingdom cannot stand."],["3:25","And if a house be divided against itself, that house cannot stand."],["3:26","And if Satan rise up against himself, and be divided, he cannot stand, but hath an end."],["3:27","No man can enter into a strong man's house, and spoil his goods, except he will first bind the strong man; and then he will spoil his house."]]},{"heading":"The Sin Not Forgiven","verses":[["3:28","Verily I say unto you, All sins shall be forgiven unto the sons of men, and blasphemies wherewith soever they shall blaspheme:"],["3:29","But he that shall blaspheme against the Holy Ghost hath never forgiveness, but is in danger of eternal damnation:"],["3:30","Because they said, He hath an unclean spirit."]]},{"heading":"My Mother and My Brothers","verses":[["3:31","There came then my brethren and my mother, and, standing without, sent unto me, calling me."],["3:32","And the multitude sat about me, and they said unto me, Behold, thy mother and thy brethren without seek for thee."],["3:33","And I answered them, saying, Who is my mother, or my brethren?"],["3:34","And I looked round about on them which sat about me, and said, Behold my mother and my brethren!"],["3:35","For whosoever shall do the will of God, the same is my brother, and my sister, and mother."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 4","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"A Farmer Goes Out Sowing","verses":[["4:1","And I began again to teach by the sea side: and there was gathered unto me a great multitude, so that I entered into a ship, and sat in the sea; and the whole multitude was by the sea on the land."],["4:2","And I taught them many things by parables, and said unto them in my doctrine,"],["4:3","Hearken; Behold, there went out a sower to sow:"],["4:4","And it came to pass, as he sowed, some fell by the way side, and the fowls of the air came and devoured it up."],["4:5","And some fell on stony ground, where it had not much earth; and immediately it sprang up, because it had no depth of earth:"],["4:6","But when the sun was up, it was scorched; and because it had no root, it withered away."],["4:7","And some fell among thorns, and the thorns grew up, and choked it, and it yielded no fruit."],["4:8","And other fell on good ground, and did yield fruit that sprang up and increased; and brought forth, some thirty, and some sixty, and some an hundred."],["4:9","And I said unto them, He that hath ears to hear, let him hear."]]},{"heading":"Let In on the Secret, Shut Out from Seeing","verses":[["4:10","And when I was alone, they that were about me with the twelve asked of me the parable."],["4:11","And I said unto them, Unto you it is given to know the mystery of the kingdom of God: but unto them that are without, all these things are done in parables:"],["4:12","That seeing they may see, and not perceive; and hearing they may hear, and not understand; lest at any time they should be converted, and their sins should be forgiven them."]]},{"heading":"What the Story Means","verses":[["4:13","And I said unto them, Know ye not this parable? and how then will ye know all parables?"],["4:14","The sower soweth the word."],["4:15","And these are they by the way side, where the word is sown; but when they have heard, Satan cometh immediately, and taketh away the word that was sown in their hearts."],["4:16","And these are they likewise which are sown on stony ground; who, when they have heard the word, immediately receive it with gladness;"],["4:17","And have no root in themselves, and so endure but for a time: afterward, when affliction or persecution ariseth for the word's sake, immediately they are offended."],["4:18","And these are they which are sown among thorns; such as hear the word,"],["4:19","And the cares of this world, and the deceitfulness of riches, and the lusts of other things entering in, choke the word, and it becometh unfruitful."],["4:20","And these are they which are sown on good ground; such as hear the word, and receive it, and bring forth fruit, some thirtyfold, some sixty, and some an hundred."]]},{"heading":"A Lamp on a Stand","verses":[["4:21","And I said unto them, Is a candle brought to be put under a bushel, or under a bed? and not to be set on a candlestick?"],["4:22","For there is nothing hid, which shall not be manifested; neither was any thing kept secret, but that it should come abroad."],["4:23","If any man have ears to hear, let him hear."]]},{"heading":"The Measure You Use","verses":[["4:24","And I said unto them, Take heed what ye hear: with what measure ye mete, it shall be measured to you: and unto you that hear shall more be given."],["4:25","For he that hath, to him shall be given: and he that hath not, from him shall be taken even that which he hath."]]},{"heading":"Seed Growing in the Dark","verses":[["4:26","And I said, So is the kingdom of God, as if a man should cast seed into the ground;"],["4:27","And should sleep, and rise night and day, and the seed should spring and grow up, he knoweth not how."],["4:28","For the earth bringeth forth fruit of herself; first the blade, then the ear, after that the full corn in the ear."],["4:29","But when the fruit is brought forth, immediately he putteth in the sickle, because the harvest is come."]]},{"heading":"The Smallest of All Seeds","verses":[["4:30","And I said, Whereunto shall we liken the kingdom of God? or with what comparison shall we compare it?"],["4:31","It is like a grain of mustard seed, which, when it is sown in the earth, is less than all the seeds that be in the earth:"],["4:32","But when it is sown, it groweth up, and becometh greater than all herbs, and shooteth out great branches; so that the fowls of the air may lodge under the shadow of it."]]},{"heading":"Explained to His Own","verses":[["4:33","And with many such parables spake I the word unto them, as they were able to hear it."],["4:34","But without a parable spake I not unto them: and when they were alone, I expounded all things to my disciples."]]},{"heading":"Peace, Be Still","verses":[["4:35","And the same day, when the even was come, I say unto them, Let us pass over unto the other side."],["4:36","And when they had sent away the multitude, they took me even as I was in the ship. And there were also with me other little ships."],["4:37","And there arose a great storm of wind, and the waves beat into the ship, so that it was now full."],["4:38","And I was in the hinder part of the ship, asleep on a pillow: and they awake me, and say unto me, Master, carest thou not that we perish?"],["4:39","And I arose, and rebuked the wind, and said unto the sea, Peace, be still. And the wind ceased, and there was a great calm."],["4:40","And I said unto them, Why are ye so fearful? how is it that ye have no faith?"],["4:41","And they feared exceedingly, and said one to another, What manner of man is this, that even the wind and the sea obey him?"]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 5","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Across the Water to the Tombs","verses":[["5:1","And we came over unto the other side of the sea, into the country of the Gadarenes."],["5:2","And when I was come out of the ship, immediately there met me out of the tombs a man with an unclean spirit,"],["5:3","Who had his dwelling among the tombs; and no man could bind him, no, not with chains:"],["5:4","Because that he had been often bound with fetters and chains, and the chains had been plucked asunder by him, and the fetters broken in pieces: neither could any man tame him."],["5:5","And always, night and day, he was in the mountains, and in the tombs, crying, and cutting himself with stones."]]},{"heading":"The Name He Gave","verses":[["5:6","But when he saw me afar off, he ran and worshipped me,"],["5:7","And cried with a loud voice, and said, What have I to do with thee, Jesus, thou Son of the most high God? I adjure thee by God, that thou torment me not."],["5:8","For I said unto him, Come out of the man, thou unclean spirit."],["5:9","And I asked him, What is thy name? And he answered, saying, My name is Legion: for we are many."],["5:10","And he besought me much that I would not send them away out of the country."]]},{"heading":"Two Thousand Down the Slope","verses":[["5:11","Now there was there nigh unto the mountains a great herd of swine feeding."],["5:12","And all the devils besought me, saying, Send us into the swine, that we may enter into them."],["5:13","And forthwith I gave them leave. And the unclean spirits went out, and entered into the swine: and the herd ran violently down a steep place into the sea, (they were about two thousand;) and were choked in the sea."]]},{"heading":"Found Sitting and Clothed","verses":[["5:14","And they that fed the swine fled, and told it in the city, and in the country. And they went out to see what it was that was done."],["5:15","And they come to me, and see him that was possessed with the devil, and had the legion, sitting, and clothed, and in his right mind: and they were afraid."],["5:16","And they that saw it told them how it befell to him that was possessed with the devil, and also concerning the swine."],["5:17","And they began to pray me to depart out of their coasts."]]},{"heading":"Go Home and Tell Them","verses":[["5:18","And when I was come into the ship, he that had been possessed with the devil prayed me that he might be with me."],["5:19","Howbeit I suffered him not, but say unto him, Go home to thy friends, and tell them how great things the Lord hath done for thee, and hath had compassion on thee."],["5:20","And he departed, and began to publish in Decapolis how great things I had done for him: and all men did marvel."]]},{"heading":"A Father at His Feet","verses":[["5:21","And when I was passed over again by ship unto the other side, much people gathered unto me: and I was nigh unto the sea."],["5:22","And, behold, there cometh one of the rulers of the synagogue, Jairus by name; and when he saw me, he fell at my feet,"],["5:23","And besought me greatly, saying, My little daughter lieth at the point of death: I pray thee, come and lay thy hands on her, that she may be healed; and she shall live."],["5:24","And I went with him; and much people followed me, and thronged me."]]},{"heading":"Twelve Years and No Help","verses":[["5:25","And a certain woman, which had an issue of blood twelve years,"],["5:26","And had suffered many things of many physicians, and had spent all that she had, and was nothing bettered, but rather grew worse,"],["5:27","When she had heard of me, came in the press behind, and touched my garment."],["5:28","For she said, If I may touch but his clothes, I shall be whole."],["5:29","And straightway the fountain of her blood was dried up; and she felt in her body that she was healed of that plague."]]},{"heading":"He Calls Her Daughter","verses":[["5:30","And I, immediately knowing in myself that virtue had gone out of me, turned me about in the press, and said, Who touched my clothes?"],["5:31","And my disciples said unto me, Thou seest the multitude thronging thee, and sayest thou, Who touched me?"],["5:32","And I looked round about to see her that had done this thing."],["5:33","But the woman fearing and trembling, knowing what was done in her, came and fell down before me, and told me all the truth."],["5:34","And I said unto her, Daughter, thy faith hath made thee whole; go in peace, and be whole of thy plague."]]},{"heading":"Do Not Be Afraid, Only Keep Trusting","verses":[["5:35","While I yet spake, there came from the ruler of the synagogue's house certain which said, Thy daughter is dead: why troublest thou the Master any further?"],["5:36","As soon as I heard the word that was spoken, I say unto the ruler of the synagogue, Be not afraid, only believe."],["5:37","And I suffered no man to follow me, save Peter, and James, and John the brother of James."]]},{"heading":"Little Girl, Get Up","verses":[["5:38","And I come to the house of the ruler of the synagogue, and see the tumult, and them that wept and wailed greatly."],["5:39","And when I was come in, I say unto them, Why make ye this ado, and weep? the damsel is not dead, but sleepeth."],["5:40","And they laughed me to scorn. But when I had put them all out, I take the father and the mother of the damsel, and them that were with me, and enter in where the damsel was lying."],["5:41","And I took the damsel by the hand, and said unto her, Talitha cumi; which is, being interpreted, Damsel, I say unto thee, arise."],["5:42","And straightway the damsel arose, and walked; for she was of the age of twelve years. And they were astonished with a great astonishment."],["5:43","And I charged them straitly that no man should know it; and I commanded that something should be given her to eat."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 6","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"No Welcome at Home","verses":[["6:1","And I went out from thence, and came into my own country; and my disciples follow me."],["6:2","And when the sabbath day was come, I began to teach in the synagogue: and many hearing me were astonished, saying, From whence hath this man these things? and what wisdom is this which is given unto him, that even such mighty works are wrought by his hands?"],["6:3","Is not this the carpenter, the son of Mary, the brother of James, and Joses, and of Juda, and Simon? and are not his sisters here with us? And they were offended at me."],["6:4","But I said unto them, A prophet is not without honour, but in his own country, and among his own kin, and in his own house."],["6:5","And I could there do no mighty work, save that I laid my hands upon a few sick folk, and healed them."],["6:6","And I marvelled because of their unbelief. And I went round about the villages, teaching."]]},{"heading":"Sent Out Two by Two","verses":[["6:7","And I called unto me the twelve, and began to send them forth by two and two; and gave them power over unclean spirits;"],["6:8","And I commanded them that they should take nothing for their journey, save a staff only; no scrip, no bread, no money in their purse:"],["6:9","But be shod with sandals; and not put on two coats."],["6:10","And I said unto them, In what place soever ye enter into an house, there abide till ye depart from that place."],["6:11","And whosoever shall not receive you, nor hear you, when ye depart thence, shake off the dust under your feet for a testimony against them. Verily I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for Sodom and Gomorrha in the day of judgment, than for that city."],["6:12","And they went out, and preached that men should repent."],["6:13","And they cast out many devils, and anointed with oil many that were sick, and healed them."]]},{"heading":"Herod Hears the Reports","verses":[["6:14","And king Herod heard of me; (for my name was spread abroad:) and he said, That John the Baptist was risen from the dead, and therefore mighty works do shew forth themselves in him."],["6:15","Others said, That it is Elias. And others said, That it is a prophet, or as one of the prophets."],["6:16","But when Herod heard thereof, he said, It is John, whom I beheaded: he is risen from the dead."]]},{"heading":"The Prophet in Prison","verses":[["6:17","For Herod himself had sent forth and laid hold upon John, and bound him in prison for Herodias' sake, his brother Philip's wife: for he had married her."],["6:18","For John had said unto Herod, It is not lawful for thee to have thy brother's wife."],["6:19","Therefore Herodias had a quarrel against him, and would have killed him; but she could not:"],["6:20","For Herod feared John, knowing that he was a just man and an holy, and observed him; and when he heard him, he did many things, and heard him gladly."]]},{"heading":"A Birthday and a Promise","verses":[["6:21","And when a convenient day was come, that Herod on his birthday made a supper to his lords, high captains, and chief estates of Galilee;"],["6:22","And when the daughter of the said Herodias came in, and danced, and pleased Herod and them that sat with him, the king said unto the damsel, Ask of me whatsoever thou wilt, and I will give it thee."],["6:23","And he sware unto her, Whatsoever thou shalt ask of me, I will give it thee, unto the half of my kingdom."],["6:24","And she went forth, and said unto her mother, What shall I ask? And she said, The head of John the Baptist."]]},{"heading":"The Head on a Platter","verses":[["6:25","And she came in straightway with haste unto the king, and asked, saying, I will that thou give me by and by in a charger the head of John the Baptist."],["6:26","And the king was exceeding sorry; yet for his oath's sake, and for their sakes which sat with him, he would not reject her."],["6:27","And immediately the king sent an executioner, and commanded his head to be brought: and he went and beheaded him in the prison,"],["6:28","And brought his head in a charger, and gave it to the damsel: and the damsel gave it to her mother."],["6:29","And when his disciples heard of it, they came and took up his corpse, and laid it in a tomb."]]},{"heading":"Come Away and Rest","verses":[["6:30","And the apostles gathered themselves together unto me, and told me all things, both what they had done, and what they had taught."],["6:31","And I said unto them, Come ye yourselves apart into a desert place, and rest a while: for there were many coming and going, and we had no leisure so much as to eat."],["6:32","And we departed into a desert place by ship privately."],["6:33","And the people saw us departing, and many knew me, and ran afoot thither out of all cities, and outwent us, and came together unto me."],["6:34","And I, when I came out, saw much people, and was moved with compassion toward them, because they were as sheep not having a shepherd: and I began to teach them many things."]]},{"heading":"Five Loaves, Two Fish","verses":[["6:35","And when the day was now far spent, my disciples came unto me, and said, This is a desert place, and now the time is far passed:"],["6:36","Send them away, that they may go into the country round about, and into the villages, and buy themselves bread: for they have nothing to eat."],["6:37","I answered and said unto them, Give ye them to eat. And they say unto me, Shall we go and buy two hundred pennyworth of bread, and give them to eat?"],["6:38","I say unto them, How many loaves have ye? go and see. And when they knew, they say, Five, and two fishes."],["6:39","And I commanded them to make all sit down by companies upon the green grass."],["6:40","And they sat down in ranks, by hundreds, and by fifties."],["6:41","And when I had taken the five loaves and the two fishes, I looked up to heaven, and blessed, and brake the loaves, and gave them to my disciples to set before them; and the two fishes divided I among them all."]]},{"heading":"Twelve Baskets Gathered Up","verses":[["6:42","And they did all eat, and were filled."],["6:43","And they took up twelve baskets full of the fragments, and of the fishes."],["6:44","And they that did eat of the loaves were about five thousand men."]]},{"heading":"He Comes Walking on the Water","verses":[["6:45","And straightway I constrained my disciples to get into the ship, and to go to the other side before unto Bethsaida, while I sent away the people."],["6:46","And when I had sent them away, I departed into a mountain to pray."],["6:47","And when even was come, the ship was in the midst of the sea, and I alone on the land."],["6:48","And I saw them toiling in rowing; for the wind was contrary unto them: and about the fourth watch of the night I come unto them, walking upon the sea, and would have passed by them."],["6:49","But when they saw me walking upon the sea, they supposed it had been a spirit, and cried out:"],["6:50","For they all saw me, and were troubled. And immediately I talked with them, and say unto them, Be of good cheer: it is I; be not afraid."],["6:51","And I went up unto them into the ship; and the wind ceased: and they were sore amazed in themselves beyond measure, and wondered."],["6:52","For they considered not the miracle of the loaves: for their heart was hardened."]]},{"heading":"Healing at Gennesaret","verses":[["6:53","And when we had passed over, we came into the land of Gennesaret, and drew to the shore."],["6:54","And when we were come out of the ship, straightway they knew me,"],["6:55","And ran through that whole region round about, and began to carry about in beds those that were sick, where they heard I was."],["6:56","And whithersoever I entered, into villages, or cities, or country, they laid the sick in the streets, and besought me that they might touch if it were but the border of my garment: and as many as touched me were made whole."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 7","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Washed Hands, Distant Hearts","verses":[["7:1","Then came together unto me the Pharisees, and certain of the scribes, which came from Jerusalem."],["7:2","And when they saw some of my disciples eat bread with defiled, that is to say, with unwashen, hands, they found fault."],["7:3","For the Pharisees, and all the Jews, except they wash their hands oft, eat not, holding the tradition of the elders."],["7:4","And when they come from the market, except they wash, they eat not. And many other things there be, which they have received to hold, as the washing of cups, and pots, brasen vessels, and of tables."],["7:5","Then the Pharisees and scribes asked me, Why walk not thy disciples according to the tradition of the elders, but eat bread with unwashen hands?"],["7:6","I answered and said unto them, Well hath Esaias prophesied of you hypocrites, as it is written, This people honoureth me with their lips, but their heart is far from me."],["7:7","Howbeit in vain do they worship me, teaching for doctrines the commandments of men."],["7:8","For laying aside the commandment of God, ye hold the tradition of men, as the washing of pots and cups: and many other such like things ye do."]]},{"heading":"Pushing Aside the Command of God","verses":[["7:9","And I said unto them, Full well ye reject the commandment of God, that ye may keep your own tradition."],["7:10","For Moses said, Honour thy father and thy mother; and, Whoso curseth father or mother, let him die the death:"],["7:11","But ye say, If a man shall say to his father or mother, It is Corban, that is to say, a gift, by whatsoever thou mightest be profited by me; he shall be free."],["7:12","And ye suffer him no more to do ought for his father or his mother;"],["7:13","Making the word of God of none effect through your tradition, which ye have delivered: and many such like things do ye."]]},{"heading":"Nothing from Outside Makes a Person Unclean","verses":[["7:14","And when I had called all the people unto me, I said unto them, Hearken unto me every one of you, and understand:"],["7:15","There is nothing from without a man, that entering into him can defile him: but the things which come out of him, those are they that defile the man."],["7:16","If any man have ears to hear, let him hear."]]},{"heading":"The Heart Is the Source","verses":[["7:17","And when I was entered into the house from the people, my disciples asked me concerning the parable."],["7:18","And I say unto them, Are ye so without understanding also? Do ye not perceive, that whatsoever thing from without entereth into the man, it cannot defile him;"],["7:19","Because it entereth not into his heart, but into the belly, and goeth out into the draught, purging all meats?"],["7:20","And I said, That which cometh out of the man, that defileth the man."],["7:21","For from within, out of the heart of men, proceed evil thoughts, adulteries, fornications, murders,"],["7:22","Thefts, covetousness, wickedness, deceit, lasciviousness, an evil eye, blasphemy, pride, foolishness:"],["7:23","All these evil things come from within, and defile the man."]]},{"heading":"A Mother Who Would Not Stop","verses":[["7:24","And from thence I arose, and went into the borders of Tyre and Sidon, and entered into an house, and would have no man know it: but I could not be hid."],["7:25","For a certain woman, whose young daughter had an unclean spirit, heard of me, and came and fell at my feet:"],["7:26","The woman was a Greek, a Syrophenician by nation; and she besought me that I would cast forth the devil out of her daughter."],["7:27","But I said unto her, Let the children first be filled: for it is not meet to take the children's bread, and to cast it unto the dogs."],["7:28","And she answered and said unto me, Yes, Lord: yet the dogs under the table eat of the children's crumbs."],["7:29","And I said unto her, For this saying go thy way; the devil is gone out of thy daughter."],["7:30","And when she was come to her house, she found the devil gone out, and her daughter laid upon the bed."]]},{"heading":"A Sigh and One Word","verses":[["7:31","And again, departing from the coasts of Tyre and Sidon, I came unto the sea of Galilee, through the midst of the coasts of Decapolis."],["7:32","And they bring unto me one that was deaf, and had an impediment in his speech; and they beseech me to put my hand upon him."],["7:33","And I took him aside from the multitude, and put my fingers into his ears, and I spit, and touched his tongue;"],["7:34","And looking up to heaven, I sighed, and say unto him, Ephphatha, that is, Be opened."],["7:35","And straightway his ears were opened, and the string of his tongue was loosed, and he spake plain."],["7:36","And I charged them that they should tell no man: but the more I charged them, so much the more a great deal they published it;"],["7:37","And were beyond measure astonished, saying, He hath done all things well: he maketh both the deaf to hear, and the dumb to speak."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 8","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Seven Loaves for Four Thousand","verses":[["8:1","In those days the multitude being very great, and having nothing to eat, I called my disciples unto me, and say unto them,"],["8:2","I have compassion on the multitude, because they have now been with me three days, and have nothing to eat:"],["8:3","And if I send them away fasting to their own houses, they will faint by the way: for divers of them came from far."],["8:4","And my disciples answered me, From whence can a man satisfy these men with bread here in the wilderness?"],["8:5","And I asked them, How many loaves have ye? And they said, Seven."],["8:6","And I commanded the people to sit down on the ground: and I took the seven loaves, and gave thanks, and brake, and gave to my disciples to set before them; and they did set them before the people."],["8:7","And they had a few small fishes: and I blessed, and commanded to set them also before them."],["8:8","So they did eat, and were filled: and they took up of the broken meat that was left seven baskets."],["8:9","And they that had eaten were about four thousand: and I sent them away."],["8:10","And straightway I entered into a ship with my disciples, and came into the parts of Dalmanutha."]]},{"heading":"No Sign for This Generation","verses":[["8:11","And the Pharisees came forth, and began to question with me, seeking of me a sign from heaven, tempting me."],["8:12","And I sighed deeply in my spirit, and say, Why doth this generation seek after a sign? verily I say unto you, There shall no sign be given unto this generation."],["8:13","And I left them, and entering into the ship again departed to the other side."]]},{"heading":"The Yeast They Could Not See","verses":[["8:14","Now my disciples had forgotten to take bread, neither had they in the ship with them more than one loaf."],["8:15","And I charged them, saying, Take heed, beware of the leaven of the Pharisees, and of the leaven of Herod."],["8:16","And they reasoned among themselves, saying, It is because we have no bread."],["8:17","And when I knew it, I say unto them, Why reason ye, because ye have no bread? perceive ye not yet, neither understand? have ye your heart yet hardened?"]]},{"heading":"Do You Still Not Understand","verses":[["8:18","Having eyes, see ye not? and having ears, hear ye not? and do ye not remember?"],["8:19","When I brake the five loaves among five thousand, how many baskets full of fragments took ye up? They say unto me, Twelve."],["8:20","And when the seven among four thousand, how many baskets full of fragments took ye up? And they said, Seven."],["8:21","And I said unto them, How is it that ye do not understand?"]]},{"heading":"Men Who Looked Like Trees","verses":[["8:22","And I come to Bethsaida; and they bring a blind man unto me, and besought me to touch him."],["8:23","And I took the blind man by the hand, and led him out of the town; and when I had spit on his eyes, and put my hands upon him, I asked him if he saw ought."],["8:24","And he looked up, and said, I see men as trees, walking."],["8:25","After that I put my hands again upon his eyes, and made him look up: and he was restored, and saw every man clearly."],["8:26","And I sent him away to his house, saying, Neither go into the town, nor tell it to any in the town."]]},{"heading":"You Are the Messiah","verses":[["8:27","And I went out, and my disciples, into the towns of Cesarea Philippi: and by the way I asked my disciples, saying unto them, Whom do men say that I am?"],["8:28","And they answered, John the Baptist: but some say, Elias; and others, One of the prophets."],["8:29","And I say unto them, But whom say ye that I am? And Peter answereth and saith unto me, Thou art the Christ."],["8:30","And I charged them that they should tell no man of me."]]},{"heading":"The Road to the Cross","verses":[["8:31","And I began to teach them, that I, the Son of man, must suffer many things, and be rejected of the elders, and of the chief priests, and scribes, and be killed, and after three days rise again."],["8:32","And I spake that saying openly. And Peter took me, and began to rebuke me."],["8:33","But when I had turned about and looked on my disciples, I rebuked Peter, saying, Get thee behind me, Satan: for thou savourest not the things that be of God, but the things that be of men."]]},{"heading":"The Terms of Following","verses":[["8:34","And when I had called the people unto me with my disciples also, I said unto them, Whosoever will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me."],["8:35","For whosoever will save his life shall lose it; but whosoever shall lose his life for my sake and the gospel's, the same shall save it."],["8:36","For what shall it profit a man, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul?"],["8:37","Or what shall a man give in exchange for his soul?"],["8:38","Whosoever therefore shall be ashamed of me and of my words in this adulterous and sinful generation; of him also shall I, the Son of man, be ashamed, when I come in the glory of my Father with the holy angels."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 9","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Transfigured Before Their Eyes","verses":[["9:1","And I said unto them, Verily I say unto you, That there be some of them that stand here, which shall not taste of death, till they have seen the kingdom of God come with power."],["9:2","And after six days I take with me Peter, and James, and John, and lead them up into an high mountain apart by themselves: and I was transfigured before them."],["9:3","And my raiment became shining, exceeding white as snow; so as no fuller on earth can white them."],["9:4","And there appeared unto them Elias with Moses: and they were talking with me."],["9:5","And Peter answered and said to me, Master, it is good for us to be here: and let us make three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias."],["9:6","For he wist not what to say; for they were sore afraid."],["9:7","And there was a cloud that overshadowed them: and a voice came out of the cloud, saying, This is my beloved Son: hear him."],["9:8","And suddenly, when they had looked round about, they saw no man any more, save me only with themselves."]]},{"heading":"Coming Down the Mountain","verses":[["9:9","And as they came down from the mountain, I charged them that they should tell no man what things they had seen, till I, the Son of man, were risen from the dead."],["9:10","And they kept that saying with themselves, questioning one with another what the rising from the dead should mean."],["9:11","And they asked me, saying, Why say the scribes that Elias must first come?"],["9:12","And I answered and told them, Elias verily cometh first, and restoreth all things; and how it is written of me, the Son of man, that I must suffer many things, and be set at nought."],["9:13","But I say unto you, That Elias is indeed come, and they have done unto him whatsoever they listed, as it is written of him."]]},{"heading":"I Do Believe","verses":[["9:14","And when I came to my disciples, I saw a great multitude about them, and the scribes questioning with them."],["9:15","And straightway all the people, when they beheld me, were greatly amazed, and running to me saluted me."],["9:16","And I asked the scribes, What question ye with them?"],["9:17","And one of the multitude answered and said, Master, I have brought unto thee my son, which hath a dumb spirit;"],["9:18","And wheresoever he taketh him, he teareth him: and he foameth, and gnasheth with his teeth, and pineth away: and I spake to thy disciples that they should cast him out; and they could not."],["9:19","I answer him, and say, O faithless generation, how long shall I be with you? how long shall I suffer you? bring him unto me."],["9:20","And they brought him unto me: and when I saw him, straightway the spirit tare him; and he fell on the ground, and wallowed foaming."],["9:21","And I asked his father, How long is it ago since this came unto him? And he said, Of a child."],["9:22","And ofttimes it hath cast him into the fire, and into the waters, to destroy him: but if thou canst do any thing, have compassion on us, and help us."],["9:23","I said unto him, If thou canst believe, all things are possible to him that believeth."],["9:24","And straightway the father of the child cried out, and said with tears, Lord, I believe; help thou mine unbelief."]]},{"heading":"The Boy Lifted Up","verses":[["9:25","When I saw that the people came running together, I rebuked the foul spirit, saying unto him, Thou dumb and deaf spirit, I charge thee, come out of him, and enter no more into him."],["9:26","And the spirit cried, and rent him sore, and came out of him: and he was as one dead; insomuch that many said, He is dead."],["9:27","But I took him by the hand, and lifted him up; and he arose."],["9:28","And when I was come into the house, my disciples asked me privately, Why could not we cast him out?"],["9:29","And I said unto them, This kind can come forth by nothing, but by prayer and fasting."]]},{"heading":"Told Again, and Afraid to Ask","verses":[["9:30","And we departed thence, and passed through Galilee; and I would not that any man should know it."],["9:31","For I taught my disciples, and said unto them, I, the Son of man, am delivered into the hands of men, and they shall kill me; and after that I am killed, I shall rise the third day."],["9:32","But they understood not that saying, and were afraid to ask me."]]},{"heading":"A Child in the Middle","verses":[["9:33","And I came to Capernaum: and being in the house I asked them, What was it that ye disputed among yourselves by the way?"],["9:34","But they held their peace: for by the way they had disputed among themselves, who should be the greatest."],["9:35","And I sat down, and called the twelve, and say unto them, If any man desire to be first, the same shall be last of all, and servant of all."],["9:36","And I took a child, and set him in the midst of them: and when I had taken him in my arms, I said unto them,"],["9:37","Whosoever shall receive one of such children in my name, receiveth me: and whosoever shall receive me, receiveth not me, but him that sent me."]]},{"heading":"Whoever Is Not Against Us","verses":[["9:38","And John answered me, saying, Master, we saw one casting out devils in thy name, and he followeth not us: and we forbad him, because he followeth not us."],["9:39","But I said, Forbid him not: for there is no man which shall do a miracle in my name, that can lightly speak evil of me."],["9:40","For he that is not against us is on our part."],["9:41","For whosoever shall give you a cup of water to drink in my name, because ye belong to Christ, verily I say unto you, he shall not lose his reward."]]},{"heading":"Better to Enter Life Maimed Than Be Thrown into Hell","verses":[["9:42","And whosoever shall offend one of these little ones that believe in me, it is better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and he were cast into the sea."],["9:43","And if thy hand offend thee, cut it off: it is better for thee to enter into life maimed, than having two hands to go into hell, into the fire that never shall be quenched:"],["9:44","Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched."],["9:45","And if thy foot offend thee, cut it off: it is better for thee to enter halt into life, than having two feet to be cast into hell, into the fire that never shall be quenched:"],["9:46","Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched."],["9:47","And if thine eye offend thee, pluck it out: it is better for thee to enter into the kingdom of God with one eye, than having two eyes to be cast into hell fire:"],["9:48","Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched."]]},{"heading":"Salt and Peace Among You","verses":[["9:49","For every one shall be salted with fire, and every sacrifice shall be salted with salt."],["9:50","Salt is good: but if the salt have lost his saltness, wherewith will ye season it? Have salt in yourselves, and have peace one with another."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 10","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"What God Has Joined","verses":[["10:1","And I arose from thence, and come into the coasts of Judea by the farther side of Jordan: and the people resort unto me again; and, as I was wont, I taught them again."],["10:2","And the Pharisees came to me, and asked me, Is it lawful for a man to put away his wife? tempting me."],["10:3","And I answered and said unto them, What did Moses command you?"],["10:4","And they said, Moses suffered to write a bill of divorcement, and to put her away."],["10:5","And I answered and said unto them, For the hardness of your heart he wrote you this precept."],["10:6","But from the beginning of the creation God made them male and female."],["10:7","For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and cleave to his wife;"],["10:8","And they twain shall be one flesh: so then they are no more twain, but one flesh."],["10:9","What therefore God hath joined together, let not man put asunder."]]},{"heading":"Alone with Him Again","verses":[["10:10","And in the house my disciples asked me again of the same matter."],["10:11","And I say unto them, Whosoever shall put away his wife, and marry another, committeth adultery against her."],["10:12","And if a woman shall put away her husband, and be married to another, she committeth adultery."]]},{"heading":"Let the Children Come","verses":[["10:13","And they brought young children to me, that I should touch them: and my disciples rebuked those that brought them."],["10:14","But when I saw it, I was much displeased, and said unto them, Suffer the little children to come unto me, and forbid them not: for of such is the kingdom of God."],["10:15","Verily I say unto you, Whosoever shall not receive the kingdom of God as a little child, he shall not enter therein."],["10:16","And I took them up in my arms, put my hands upon them, and blessed them."]]},{"heading":"He Looked at Him with Love","verses":[["10:17","And when I was gone forth into the way, there came one running, and kneeled to me, and asked me, Good Master, what shall I do that I may inherit eternal life?"],["10:18","And I said unto him, Why callest thou me good? there is none good but one, that is, God."],["10:19","Thou knowest the commandments, Do not commit adultery, Do not kill, Do not steal, Do not bear false witness, Defraud not, Honour thy father and mother."],["10:20","And he answered and said unto me, Master, all these have I observed from my youth."],["10:21","Then I, beholding him, loved him, and said unto him, One thing thou lackest: go thy way, sell whatsoever thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come, take up the cross, and follow me."],["10:22","And he was sad at that saying, and went away grieved: for he had great possessions."]]},{"heading":"Impossible for Us, Possible with God","verses":[["10:23","And I looked round about, and say unto my disciples, How hardly shall they that have riches enter into the kingdom of God!"],["10:24","And the disciples were astonished at my words. But I answer again, and say unto them, Children, how hard is it for them that trust in riches to enter into the kingdom of God!"],["10:25","It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God."],["10:26","And they were astonished out of measure, saying among themselves, Who then can be saved?"],["10:27","And I, looking upon them, say, With men it is impossible, but not with God: for with God all things are possible."]]},{"heading":"A Hundred Times as Much","verses":[["10:28","Then Peter began to say unto me, Lo, we have left all, and have followed thee."],["10:29","And I answered and said, Verily I say unto you, There is no man that hath left house, or brethren, or sisters, or father, or mother, or wife, or children, or lands, for my sake, and the gospel's,"],["10:30","But he shall receive an hundredfold now in this time, houses, and brethren, and sisters, and mothers, and children, and lands, with persecutions; and in the world to come eternal life."],["10:31","But many that are first shall be last; and the last first."]]},{"heading":"Walking Ahead on the Road","verses":[["10:32","And they were in the way going up to Jerusalem; and I went before them: and they were amazed; and as they followed, they were afraid. And I took again the twelve, and began to tell them what things should happen unto me,"],["10:33","Saying, Behold, we go up to Jerusalem; and I, the Son of man, shall be delivered unto the chief priests, and unto the scribes; and they shall condemn me to death, and shall deliver me to the Gentiles:"],["10:34","And they shall mock me, and shall scourge me, and shall spit upon me, and shall kill me: and the third day I shall rise again."]]},{"heading":"The Cup and the Baptism","verses":[["10:35","And James and John, the sons of Zebedee, come unto me, saying, Master, we would that thou shouldest do for us whatsoever we shall desire."],["10:36","And I said unto them, What would ye that I should do for you?"],["10:37","They said unto me, Grant unto us that we may sit, one on thy right hand, and the other on thy left hand, in thy glory."],["10:38","But I said unto them, Ye know not what ye ask: can ye drink of the cup that I drink of? and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with?"],["10:39","And they said unto me, We can. And I said unto them, Ye shall indeed drink of the cup that I drink of; and with the baptism that I am baptized withal shall ye be baptized:"],["10:40","But to sit on my right hand and on my left hand is not mine to give; but it shall be given to them for whom it is prepared."]]},{"heading":"A Ransom for Many","verses":[["10:41","And when the ten heard it, they began to be much displeased with James and John."],["10:42","But I called them to me, and say unto them, Ye know that they which are accounted to rule over the Gentiles exercise lordship over them; and their great ones exercise authority upon them."],["10:43","But so shall it not be among you: but whosoever will be great among you, shall be your minister:"],["10:44","And whosoever of you will be the chiefest, shall be servant of all."],["10:45","For even I, the Son of man, came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give my life a ransom for many."]]},{"heading":"Bartimaeus Throws Off His Cloak","verses":[["10:46","And we came to Jericho: and as I went out of Jericho with my disciples and a great number of people, blind Bartimeus, the son of Timeus, sat by the highway side begging."],["10:47","And when he heard that it was Jesus of Nazareth, he began to cry out, and say, Jesus, thou Son of David, have mercy on me."],["10:48","And many charged him that he should hold his peace: but he cried the more a great deal, Thou Son of David, have mercy on me."],["10:49","And I stood still, and commanded him to be called. And they call the blind man, saying unto him, Be of good comfort, rise; he calleth thee."],["10:50","And he, casting away his garment, rose, and came to me."],["10:51","And I answered and said unto him, What wilt thou that I should do unto thee? The blind man said unto me, Lord, that I might receive my sight."],["10:52","And I said unto him, Go thy way; thy faith hath made thee whole. And immediately he received his sight, and followed me in the way."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 11","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Go and Find the Colt","verses":[["11:1","And when we came nigh to Jerusalem, unto Bethphage and Bethany, at the mount of Olives, I send forth two of my disciples,"],["11:2","And say unto them, Go your way into the village over against you: and as soon as ye be entered into it, ye shall find a colt tied, whereon never man sat; loose him, and bring him."],["11:3","And if any man say unto you, Why do ye this? say ye that the Lord hath need of him; and straightway he will send him hither."],["11:4","And they went their way, and found the colt tied by the door without in a place where two ways met; and they loose him."],["11:5","And certain of them that stood there said unto them, What do ye, loosing the colt?"],["11:6","And they said unto them even as I had commanded: and they let them go."]]},{"heading":"Hosanna in the Highest","verses":[["11:7","And they brought the colt to me, and cast their garments on him; and I sat upon him."],["11:8","And many spread their garments in the way: and others cut down branches off the trees, and strawed them in the way."],["11:9","And they that went before, and they that followed, cried, saying, Hosanna; Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord:"],["11:10","Blessed be the kingdom of our father David, that cometh in the name of the Lord: Hosanna in the highest."],["11:11","And I entered into Jerusalem, and into the temple: and when I had looked round about upon all things, and now the eventide was come, I went out unto Bethany with the twelve."]]},{"heading":"A Fig Tree with Only Leaves","verses":[["11:12","And on the morrow, when we were come from Bethany, I was hungry:"],["11:13","And seeing a fig tree afar off having leaves, I came, if haply I might find any thing thereon: and when I came to it, I found nothing but leaves; for the time of figs was not yet."],["11:14","And I answered and said unto it, No man eat fruit of thee hereafter for ever. And my disciples heard it."]]},{"heading":"A House of Prayer, a Hideout for Thieves","verses":[["11:15","And we come to Jerusalem: and I went into the temple, and began to cast out them that sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold doves;"],["11:16","And would not suffer that any man should carry any vessel through the temple."],["11:17","And I taught, saying unto them, Is it not written, My house shall be called of all nations the house of prayer? but ye have made it a den of thieves."],["11:18","And the scribes and chief priests heard it, and sought how they might destroy me: for they feared me, because all the people was astonished at my doctrine."],["11:19","And when even was come, I went out of the city."]]},{"heading":"Withered to the Roots","verses":[["11:20","And in the morning, as we passed by, we saw the fig tree dried up from the roots."],["11:21","And Peter calling to remembrance saith unto me, Master, behold, the fig tree which thou cursedst is withered away."],["11:22","And I, answering, say unto them, Have faith in God."],["11:23","For verily I say unto you, That whosoever shall say unto this mountain, Be thou removed, and be thou cast into the sea; and shall not doubt in his heart, but shall believe that those things which he saith shall come to pass; he shall have whatsoever he saith."],["11:24","Therefore I say unto you, What things soever ye desire, when ye pray, believe that ye receive them, and ye shall have them."],["11:25","And when ye stand praying, forgive, if ye have ought against any: that your Father also which is in heaven may forgive you your trespasses."],["11:26","But if ye do not forgive, neither will your Father which is in heaven forgive your trespasses."]]},{"heading":"By What Authority","verses":[["11:27","And we come again to Jerusalem: and as I was walking in the temple, there come to me the chief priests, and the scribes, and the elders,"],["11:28","And say unto me, By what authority doest thou these things? and who gave thee this authority to do these things?"],["11:29","And I answered and said unto them, I will also ask of you one question, and answer me, and I will tell you by what authority I do these things."],["11:30","The baptism of John, was it from heaven, or of men? answer me."],["11:31","And they reasoned with themselves, saying, If we shall say, From heaven; he will say, Why then did ye not believe him?"],["11:32","But if we shall say, Of men; they feared the people: for all men counted John, that he was a prophet indeed."],["11:33","And they answered and said unto me, We cannot tell. And I, answering, say unto them, Neither do I tell you by what authority I do these things."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 12","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"The Vineyard and the Son","verses":[["12:1","And I began to speak unto them by parables. A certain man planted a vineyard, and set an hedge about it, and digged a place for the winefat, and built a tower, and let it out to husbandmen, and went into a far country."],["12:2","And at the season he sent to the husbandmen a servant, that he might receive from the husbandmen of the fruit of the vineyard."],["12:3","And they caught him, and beat him, and sent him away empty."],["12:4","And again he sent unto them another servant; and at him they cast stones, and wounded him in the head, and sent him away shamefully handled."],["12:5","And again he sent another; and him they killed, and many others; beating some, and killing some."],["12:6","Having yet therefore one son, his wellbeloved, he sent him also last unto them, saying, They will reverence my son."],["12:7","But those husbandmen said among themselves, This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and the inheritance shall be ours."],["12:8","And they took him, and killed him, and cast him out of the vineyard."]]},{"heading":"The Stone the Builders Threw Aside","verses":[["12:9","What shall therefore the lord of the vineyard do? he will come and destroy the husbandmen, and will give the vineyard unto others."],["12:10","And have ye not read this scripture; The stone which the builders rejected is become the head of the corner:"],["12:11","This was the Lord's doing, and it is marvellous in our eyes?"],["12:12","And they sought to lay hold on me, but feared the people: for they knew that I had spoken the parable against them: and they left me, and went their way."]]},{"heading":"Whose Face Is on the Coin","verses":[["12:13","And they send unto me certain of the Pharisees and of the Herodians, to catch me in my words."],["12:14","And when they were come, they say unto me, Master, we know that thou art true, and carest for no man: for thou regardest not the person of men, but teachest the way of God in truth: Is it lawful to give tribute to Cesar, or not?"],["12:15","Shall we give, or shall we not give? But I, knowing their hypocrisy, said unto them, Why tempt ye me? bring me a penny, that I may see it."],["12:16","And they brought it. And I say unto them, Whose is this image and superscription? And they said unto me, Cesar's."],["12:17","And I, answering, said unto them, Render to Cesar the things that are Cesar's, and to God the things that are God's. And they marvelled at me."]]},{"heading":"Seven Brothers and One Widow","verses":[["12:18","Then come unto me the Sadducees, which say there is no resurrection; and they asked me, saying,"],["12:19","Master, Moses wrote unto us, If a man's brother die, and leave his wife behind him, and leave no children, that his brother should take his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother."],["12:20","Now there were seven brethren: and the first took a wife, and dying left no seed."],["12:21","And the second took her, and died, neither left he any seed: and the third likewise."],["12:22","And the seven had her, and left no seed: last of all the woman died also."],["12:23","In the resurrection therefore, when they shall rise, whose wife shall she be of them? for the seven had her to wife."]]},{"heading":"God of the Living","verses":[["12:24","And I, answering, said unto them, Do ye not therefore err, because ye know not the scriptures, neither the power of God?"],["12:25","For when they shall rise from the dead, they neither marry, nor are given in marriage; but are as the angels which are in heaven."],["12:26","And as touching the dead, that they rise: have ye not read in the book of Moses, how in the bush God spake unto him, saying, I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob?"],["12:27","He is not the God of the dead, but the God of the living: ye therefore do greatly err."]]},{"heading":"The Greatest Commandment","verses":[["12:28","And one of the scribes came, and having heard them reasoning together, and perceiving that I had answered them well, asked me, Which is the first commandment of all?"],["12:29","And I answered him, The first of all the commandments is, Hear, O Israel; The Lord our God is one Lord:"],["12:30","And thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind, and with all thy strength: this is the first commandment."],["12:31","And the second is like, namely this, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself. There is none other commandment greater than these."],["12:32","And the scribe said unto me, Well, Master, thou hast said the truth: for there is one God; and there is none other but he:"],["12:33","And to love him with all the heart, and with all the understanding, and with all the soul, and with all the strength, and to love his neighbour as himself, is more than all whole burnt offerings and sacrifices."],["12:34","And when I saw that he answered discreetly, I said unto him, Thou art not far from the kingdom of God. And no man after that durst ask me any question."]]},{"heading":"David Calls Him Lord","verses":[["12:35","And I answered and said, while I taught in the temple, How say the scribes that Christ is the Son of David?"],["12:36","For David himself said by the Holy Ghost, The Lord said to my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool."],["12:37","David therefore himself calleth him Lord; and whence is he then his son? And the common people heard me gladly."]]},{"heading":"They Eat Up the Houses of Widows","verses":[["12:38","And I said unto them in my doctrine, Beware of the scribes, which love to go in long clothing, and love salutations in the marketplaces,"],["12:39","And the chief seats in the synagogues, and the uppermost rooms at feasts:"],["12:40","Which devour widows' houses, and for a pretence make long prayers: these shall receive greater damnation."]]},{"heading":"All She Had to Live On","verses":[["12:41","And I sat over against the treasury, and beheld how the people cast money into the treasury: and many that were rich cast in much."],["12:42","And there came a certain poor widow, and she threw in two mites, which make a farthing."],["12:43","And I called unto me my disciples, and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, That this poor widow hath cast more in, than all they which have cast into the treasury:"],["12:44","For all they did cast in of their abundance; but she of her want did cast in all that she had, even all her living."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 13","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Not One Stone Left","verses":[["13:1","And as I went out of the temple, one of my disciples saith unto me, Master, see what manner of stones and what buildings are here!"],["13:2","And I, answering, said unto him, Seest thou these great buildings? there shall not be left one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down."]]},{"heading":"Only the First Pains of Birth","verses":[["13:3","And as I sat upon the mount of Olives over against the temple, Peter and James and John and Andrew asked me privately,"],["13:4","Tell us, when shall these things be? and what shall be the sign when all these things shall be fulfilled?"],["13:5","And I, answering them, began to say, Take heed lest any man deceive you:"],["13:6","For many shall come in my name, saying, I am Christ; and shall deceive many."],["13:7","And when ye shall hear of wars and rumours of wars, be ye not troubled: for such things must needs be; but the end shall not be yet."],["13:8","For nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom: and there shall be earthquakes in divers places, and there shall be famines and troubles: these are the beginnings of sorrows."]]},{"heading":"When You Are Handed Over","verses":[["13:9","But take heed to yourselves: for they shall deliver you up to councils; and in the synagogues ye shall be beaten: and ye shall be brought before rulers and kings for my sake, for a testimony against them."],["13:10","And the gospel must first be published among all nations."],["13:11","But when they shall lead you, and deliver you up, take no thought beforehand what ye shall speak, neither do ye premeditate: but whatsoever shall be given you in that hour, that speak ye: for it is not ye that speak, but the Holy Ghost."],["13:12","Now the brother shall betray the brother to death, and the father the son; and children shall rise up against their parents, and shall cause them to be put to death."],["13:13","And ye shall be hated of all men for my name's sake: but he that shall endure unto the end, the same shall be saved."]]},{"heading":"The Days of Distress","verses":[["13:14","But when ye shall see the abomination of desolation, spoken of by Daniel the prophet, standing where it ought not, (let him that readeth understand,) then let them that be in Judea flee to the mountains:"],["13:15","And let him that is on the housetop not go down into the house, neither enter therein, to take any thing out of his house:"],["13:16","And let him that is in the field not turn back again for to take up his garment."],["13:17","But woe to them that are with child, and to them that give suck in those days!"],["13:18","And pray ye that your flight be not in the winter."],["13:19","For in those days shall be affliction, such as was not from the beginning of the creation which God created unto this time, neither shall be."],["13:20","And except that the Lord had shortened those days, no flesh should be saved: but for the elect's sake, whom he hath chosen, he hath shortened the days."]]},{"heading":"Do Not Be Misled","verses":[["13:21","And then if any man shall say to you, Lo, here is Christ; or, lo, he is there; believe him not:"],["13:22","For false Christs and false prophets shall rise, and shall shew signs and wonders, to seduce, if it were possible, even the elect."],["13:23","But take ye heed: behold, I have foretold you all things."]]},{"heading":"The Son of Man Comes","verses":[["13:24","But in those days, after that tribulation, the sun shall be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light,"],["13:25","And the stars of heaven shall fall, and the powers that are in heaven shall be shaken."],["13:26","And then shall they see me, the Son of man, coming in the clouds with great power and glory."],["13:27","And then shall I send my angels, and shall gather together my elect from the four winds, from the uttermost part of the earth to the uttermost part of heaven."]]},{"heading":"The Lesson of the Fig Tree","verses":[["13:28","Now learn a parable of the fig tree; When her branch is yet tender, and putteth forth leaves, ye know that summer is near:"],["13:29","So ye in like manner, when ye shall see these things come to pass, know that it is nigh, even at the doors."],["13:30","Verily I say unto you, that this generation shall not pass, till all these things be done."],["13:31","Heaven and earth shall pass away: but my words shall not pass away."]]},{"heading":"No One Knows the Hour","verses":[["13:32","But of that day and that hour knoweth no man, no, not the angels which are in heaven, neither I, the Son, but my Father."],["13:33","Take ye heed, watch and pray: for ye know not when the time is."],["13:34","For the Son of man is as a man taking a far journey, who left his house, and gave authority to his servants, and to every man his work, and commanded the porter to watch."],["13:35","Watch ye therefore: for ye know not when the master of the house cometh, at even, or at midnight, or at the cockcrowing, or in the morning:"],["13:36","Lest coming suddenly he find you sleeping."],["13:37","And what I say unto you I say unto all, Watch."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 14","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Two Days Before the Passover","verses":[["14:1","After two days was the feast of the passover, and of unleavened bread: and the chief priests and the scribes sought how they might take me by craft, and put me to death."],["14:2","But they said, Not on the feast day, lest there be an uproar of the people."]]},{"heading":"The Jar Broken Open","verses":[["14:3","And being in Bethany in the house of Simon the leper, as I sat at meat, there came a woman having an alabaster box of ointment of spikenard very precious; and she brake the box, and poured it on my head."],["14:4","And there were some that had indignation within themselves, and said, Why was this waste of the ointment made?"],["14:5","For it might have been sold for more than three hundred pence, and have been given to the poor. And they murmured against her."],["14:6","And I said, Let her alone; why trouble ye her? she hath wrought a good work on me."],["14:7","For ye have the poor with you always, and whensoever ye will ye may do them good: but me ye have not always."],["14:8","She hath done what she could: she is come aforehand to anoint my body to the burying."],["14:9","Verily I say unto you, Wheresoever this gospel shall be preached throughout the whole world, this also that she hath done shall be spoken of for a memorial of her."]]},{"heading":"Judas Goes to the Priests","verses":[["14:10","And Judas Iscariot, one of the twelve, went unto the chief priests, to betray me unto them."],["14:11","And when they heard it, they were glad, and promised to give him money. And he sought how he might conveniently betray me."]]},{"heading":"The Upper Room Ready","verses":[["14:12","And the first day of unleavened bread, when they killed the passover, my disciples said unto me, Where wilt thou that we go and prepare that thou mayest eat the passover?"],["14:13","And I send forth two of my disciples, and say unto them, Go ye into the city, and there shall meet you a man bearing a pitcher of water: follow him."],["14:14","And wheresoever he shall go in, say ye to the goodman of the house, The Master saith, Where is the guestchamber, where I shall eat the passover with my disciples?"],["14:15","And he will shew you a large upper room furnished and prepared: there make ready for us."],["14:16","And my disciples went forth, and came into the city, and found as I had said unto them: and they made ready the passover."]]},{"heading":"One Who Eats with Me","verses":[["14:17","And in the evening I come with the twelve."],["14:18","And as we sat and did eat, I said, Verily I say unto you, One of you which eateth with me shall betray me."],["14:19","And they began to be sorrowful, and to say unto me one by one, Is it I? and another said, Is it I?"],["14:20","And I answered and said unto them, It is one of the twelve, that dippeth with me in the dish."],["14:21","I, the Son of man, indeed go, as it is written of me: but woe to that man by whom I, the Son of man, am betrayed! good were it for that man if he had never been born."]]},{"heading":"The Bread and the Cup","verses":[["14:22","And as we did eat, I took bread, and blessed, and brake it, and gave to them, and said, Take, eat: this is my body."],["14:23","And I took the cup, and when I had given thanks, I gave it to them: and they all drank of it."],["14:24","And I said unto them, This is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many."],["14:25","Verily I say unto you, I will drink no more of the fruit of the vine, until that day that I drink it new in the kingdom of God."],["14:26","And when we had sung an hymn, we went out into the mount of Olives."]]},{"heading":"Before the Rooster Crows Twice","verses":[["14:27","And I say unto them, All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep shall be scattered."],["14:28","But after that I am risen, I will go before you into Galilee."],["14:29","But Peter said unto me, Although all shall be offended, yet will not I."],["14:30","And I say unto him, Verily I say unto thee, That this day, even in this night, before the cock crow twice, thou shalt deny me thrice."],["14:31","But he spake the more vehemently, If I should die with thee, I will not deny thee in any wise. Likewise also said they all."]]},{"heading":"Abba, Father","verses":[["14:32","And we came to a place which was named Gethsemane: and I say to my disciples, Sit ye here, while I shall pray."],["14:33","And I take with me Peter and James and John, and began to be sore amazed, and to be very heavy;"],["14:34","And say unto them, My soul is exceeding sorrowful unto death: tarry ye here, and watch."],["14:35","And I went forward a little, and fell on the ground, and prayed that, if it were possible, the hour might pass from me."],["14:36","And I said, Abba, Father, all things are possible unto thee; take away this cup from me: nevertheless not what I will, but what thou wilt."]]},{"heading":"Could You Not Keep Watch","verses":[["14:37","And I come, and find them sleeping, and say unto Peter, Simon, sleepest thou? couldest not thou watch one hour?"],["14:38","Watch ye and pray, lest ye enter into temptation. The spirit truly is ready, but the flesh is weak."],["14:39","And again I went away, and prayed, and spake the same words."],["14:40","And when I returned, I found them asleep again, (for their eyes were heavy,) neither wist they what to answer me."],["14:41","And I come the third time, and say unto them, Sleep on now, and take your rest: it is enough, the hour is come; behold, I, the Son of man, am betrayed into the hands of sinners."],["14:42","Rise up, let us go; lo, he that betrayeth me is at hand."]]},{"heading":"The Signal Was a Kiss","verses":[["14:43","And immediately, while I yet spake, cometh Judas, one of the twelve, and with him a great multitude with swords and staves, from the chief priests and the scribes and the elders."],["14:44","And he that betrayed me had given them a token, saying, Whomsoever I shall kiss, that same is he; take him, and lead him away safely."],["14:45","And as soon as he was come, he goeth straightway to me, and saith, Master, master; and kissed me."],["14:46","And they laid their hands on me, and took me."]]},{"heading":"They All Ran Away","verses":[["14:47","And one of them that stood by drew a sword, and smote a servant of the high priest, and cut off his ear."],["14:48","And I answered and said unto them, Are ye come out, as against a thief, with swords and with staves to take me?"],["14:49","I was daily with you in the temple teaching, and ye took me not: but the scriptures must be fulfilled."],["14:50","And they all forsook me, and fled."],["14:51","And there followed me a certain young man, having a linen cloth cast about his naked body; and the young men laid hold on him:"],["14:52","And he left the linen cloth, and fled from them naked."]]},{"heading":"The Council Finds No Case","verses":[["14:53","And they led me away to the high priest: and with him were assembled all the chief priests and the elders and the scribes."],["14:54","And Peter followed me afar off, even into the palace of the high priest: and he sat with the servants, and warmed himself at the fire."],["14:55","And the chief priests and all the council sought for witness against me to put me to death; and found none."],["14:56","For many bare false witness against me, but their witness agreed not together."],["14:57","And there arose certain, and bare false witness against me, saying,"],["14:58","We heard him say, I will destroy this temple that is made with hands, and within three days I will build another made without hands."],["14:59","But neither so did their witness agree together."]]},{"heading":"I Am","verses":[["14:60","And the high priest stood up in the midst, and asked me, saying, Answerest thou nothing? what is it which these witness against thee?"],["14:61","But I held my peace, and answered nothing. Again the high priest asked me, and said unto me, Art thou the Christ, the Son of the Blessed?"],["14:62","And I said, I am: and ye shall see me, the Son of man, sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven."],["14:63","Then the high priest rent his clothes, and saith, What need we any further witnesses?"],["14:64","Ye have heard the blasphemy: what think ye? And they all condemned me to be guilty of death."],["14:65","And some began to spit on me, and to cover my face, and to buffet me, and to say unto me, Prophesy: and the servants did strike me with the palms of their hands."]]},{"heading":"Peter and the Rooster","verses":[["14:66","And as Peter was beneath in the palace, there cometh one of the maids of the high priest:"],["14:67","And when she saw Peter warming himself, she looked upon him, and said, And thou also wast with Jesus of Nazareth."],["14:68","But he denied, saying, I know not, neither understand I what thou sayest. And he went out into the porch; and the cock crew."],["14:69","And a maid saw him again, and began to say to them that stood by, This is one of them."],["14:70","And he denied it again. And a little after, they that stood by said again to Peter, Surely thou art one of them: for thou art a Galilean, and thy speech agreeth thereto."],["14:71","But he began to curse and to swear, saying, I know not this man of whom ye speak."],["14:72","And the second time the cock crew. And Peter called to mind the word that I said unto him, Before the cock crow twice, thou shalt deny me thrice. And when he thought thereon, he wept."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 15","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Standing Before Pilate","verses":[["15:1","And straightway in the morning the chief priests held a consultation with the elders and scribes and the whole council, and bound me, and carried me away, and delivered me to Pilate."],["15:2","And Pilate asked me, Art thou the King of the Jews? And I, answering, said unto him, Thou sayest it."],["15:3","And the chief priests accused me of many things: but I answered nothing."],["15:4","And Pilate asked me again, saying, Answerest thou nothing? behold how many things they witness against thee."],["15:5","But I yet answered nothing; so that Pilate marvelled."]]},{"heading":"The Crowd Asks for Barabbas","verses":[["15:6","Now at that feast he released unto them one prisoner, whomsoever they desired."],["15:7","And there was one named Barabbas, which lay bound with them that had made insurrection with him, who had committed murder in the insurrection."],["15:8","And the multitude crying aloud began to desire him to do as he had ever done unto them."],["15:9","But Pilate answered them, saying, Will ye that I release unto you the King of the Jews?"],["15:10","For he knew that the chief priests had delivered me for envy."],["15:11","But the chief priests moved the people, that he should rather release Barabbas unto them."]]},{"heading":"Pilate Gives the Order","verses":[["15:12","And Pilate answered and said again unto them, What will ye then that I shall do unto him whom ye call the King of the Jews?"],["15:13","And they cried out again, Crucify him."],["15:14","Then Pilate said unto them, Why, what evil hath he done? And they cried out the more exceedingly, Crucify him."],["15:15","And so Pilate, willing to content the people, released Barabbas unto them, and delivered me, when he had scourged me, to be crucified."]]},{"heading":"The Purple Robe","verses":[["15:16","And the soldiers led me away into the hall, called Pretorium; and they call together the whole band."],["15:17","And they clothed me with purple, and platted a crown of thorns, and put it about my head,"],["15:18","And began to salute me, Hail, King of the Jews!"],["15:19","And they smote me on the head with a reed, and did spit upon me, and bowing their knees worshipped me."],["15:20","And when they had mocked me, they took off the purple from me, and put my own clothes on me, and led me out to crucify me."]]},{"heading":"Simon Carries the Cross","verses":[["15:21","And they compel one Simon a Cyrenian, who passed by, coming out of the country, the father of Alexander and Rufus, to bear my cross."],["15:22","And they bring me unto the place Golgotha, which is, being interpreted, The place of a skull."],["15:23","And they gave me to drink wine mingled with myrrh: but I received it not."],["15:24","And when they had crucified me, they parted my garments, casting lots upon them, what every man should take."]]},{"heading":"The Charge Written Above Him","verses":[["15:25","And it was the third hour, and they crucified me."],["15:26","And the superscription of my accusation was written over, THE KING OF THE JEWS."],["15:27","And with me they crucify two thieves; the one on my right hand, and the other on my left."],["15:28","And the scripture was fulfilled, which saith, And he was numbered with the transgressors."]]},{"heading":"Save Yourself and Come Down","verses":[["15:29","And they that passed by railed on me, wagging their heads, and saying, Ah, thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest it in three days,"],["15:30","Save thyself, and come down from the cross."],["15:31","Likewise also the chief priests mocking said among themselves with the scribes, He saved others; himself he cannot save."],["15:32","Let Christ the King of Israel descend now from the cross, that we may see and believe. And they that were crucified with me reviled me."]]},{"heading":"Darkness at Midday","verses":[["15:33","And when the sixth hour was come, there was darkness over the whole land until the ninth hour."],["15:34","And at the ninth hour I cried with a loud voice, saying, Eloi, Eloi, lama sabachthani? which is, being interpreted, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?"],["15:35","And some of them that stood by, when they heard it, said, Behold, he calleth Elias."],["15:36","And one ran and filled a spunge full of vinegar, and put it on a reed, and gave me to drink, saying, Let alone; let us see whether Elias will come to take him down."]]},{"heading":"The Curtain Torn Open","verses":[["15:37","And I cried with a loud voice, and gave up the ghost."],["15:38","And the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom."],["15:39","And when the centurion, which stood over against me, saw that I so cried out, and gave up the ghost, he said, Truly this man was the Son of God."]]},{"heading":"The Women Watching from Afar","verses":[["15:40","There were also women looking on afar off: among whom was Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James the less and of Joses, and Salome;"],["15:41","(Who also, when I was in Galilee, followed me, and ministered unto me;) and many other women which came up with me unto Jerusalem."]]},{"heading":"Joseph of Arimathea","verses":[["15:42","And now when the even was come, because it was the preparation, that is, the day before the sabbath,"],["15:43","Joseph of Arimathea, an honourable counsellor, which also waited for the kingdom of God, came, and went in boldly unto Pilate, and craved my body."],["15:44","And Pilate marvelled if I were already dead: and calling unto him the centurion, he asked him whether I had been any while dead."],["15:45","And when he knew it of the centurion, he gave my body to Joseph."],["15:46","And he bought fine linen, and took me down, and wrapped me in the linen, and laid me in a sepulchre which was hewn out of a rock, and rolled a stone unto the door of the sepulchre."],["15:47","And Mary Magdalene and Mary the mother of Joses beheld where I was laid."]]}]},{"ref":"Mark 16","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"The Stone Already Rolled Back","verses":[["16:1","And when the sabbath was past, Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James, and Salome, had bought sweet spices, that they might come and anoint me."],["16:2","And very early in the morning the first day of the week, they came unto the sepulchre at the rising of the sun."],["16:3","And they said among themselves, Who shall roll us away the stone from the door of the sepulchre?"],["16:4","And when they looked, they saw that the stone was rolled away: for it was very great."]]},{"heading":"He Has Risen","verses":[["16:5","And entering into the sepulchre, they saw a young man sitting on the right side, clothed in a long white garment; and they were affrighted."],["16:6","And he saith unto them, Be not affrighted: Ye seek Jesus of Nazareth, which was crucified: he is risen; he is not here: behold the place where they laid him."],["16:7","But go your way, tell his disciples and Peter that he goeth before you into Galilee: there shall ye see him, as he said unto you."],["16:8","And they went out quickly, and fled from the sepulchre; for they trembled and were amazed: neither said they any thing to any man; for they were afraid."]]},{"heading":"First to Mary Magdalene","verses":[["16:9","Now when I was risen early the first day of the week, I appeared first to Mary Magdalene, out of whom I had cast seven devils."],["16:10","And she went and told them that had been with me, as they mourned and wept."],["16:11","And they, when they had heard that I was alive, and had been seen of her, believed not."]]},{"heading":"Two on the Road","verses":[["16:12","After that I appeared in another form unto two of them, as they walked, and went into the country."],["16:13","And they went and told it unto the residue: neither believed they them."],["16:14","Afterward I appeared unto the eleven as they sat at meat, and upbraided them with their unbelief and hardness of heart, because they believed not them which had seen me after I was risen."]]},{"heading":"Go Out into the Whole World","verses":[["16:15","And I said unto them, Go ye into all the world, and preach the gospel to every creature."],["16:16","He that believeth and is baptized shall be saved; but he that believeth not shall be damned."],["16:17","And these signs shall follow them that believe; In my name shall they cast out devils; they shall speak with new tongues;"],["16:18","They shall take up serpents; and if they drink any deadly thing, it shall not hurt them; they shall lay hands on the sick, and they shall recover."]]},{"heading":"Working Along with Them","verses":[["16:19","So then after I had spoken unto them, I was received up into heaven, and sat on the right hand of God."],["16:20","And they went forth, and preached every where, I working with them, and confirming the word with signs following. Amen."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 1","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"A Servant Sent with Good News","verses":[["1:1","Paul, a servant of mine, called to be an apostle, separated unto the gospel of my Father,"],["1:2","(Which my Father had promised afore by his prophets in the holy scriptures,)"],["1:3","Concerning me, his Son, Jesus Christ your Lord, which was made of the seed of David according to the flesh;"],["1:4","And declared to be the Son of my Father with power, according to the spirit of holiness, by my resurrection from the dead:"],["1:5","By me Paul received grace and apostleship, for obedience to the faith among all nations, for my name:"],["1:6","Among whom are ye also called by me:"],["1:7","To all that be in Rome, beloved of my Father, called to be saints: Grace to you and peace from my Father, and from me, the Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{"heading":"Longing to Come to Rome","verses":[["1:8","First, Paul thanked my Father through me for you all, that your faith is spoken of throughout the whole world."],["1:9","For my Father is Paul's witness, whom he serveth with his spirit in the gospel concerning me, that without ceasing he maketh mention of you always in his prayers;"],["1:10","Making request, if by any means now at length he might have a prosperous journey by the will of my Father to come unto you."],["1:11","For Paul longed to see you, that he might impart unto you some spiritual gift, to the end ye may be established;"],["1:12","That is, that he might be comforted together with you by the mutual faith both of you and him."],["1:13","Now Paul would not have you ignorant, brethren, that oftentimes he purposed to come unto you, (but was let hitherto,) that he might have some fruit among you also, even as among other Gentiles."],["1:14","Paul was debtor both to the Greeks, and to the Barbarians; both to the wise, and to the unwise."],["1:15","So, as much as in him was, Paul was ready to preach the gospel to you that are at Rome also."]]},{"heading":"The Power of God for Everyone","verses":[["1:16","For Paul was not ashamed of the gospel concerning me: for it is the power of my Father unto salvation to every one that believeth; to the Jew first, and also to the Greek."],["1:17","For therein is the righteousness of my Father revealed from faith to faith: as it is written, The just shall live by faith."]]},{"heading":"The Wrath Revealed, and What Creation Makes Plain","verses":[["1:18","For the wrath of my Father is revealed from heaven against all ungodliness and unrighteousness of men, who hold the truth in unrighteousness;"],["1:19","Because that which may be known of my Father is manifest in them; for my Father hath shewed it unto them."],["1:20","For the invisible things of him from the creation of the world are clearly seen, being understood by the things that are made, even his eternal power and Godhead; so that they are without excuse:"],["1:21","Because that, when they knew my Father, they glorified him not as my Father, neither were thankful; but became vain in their imaginations, and their foolish heart was darkened."],["1:22","Professing themselves to be wise, they became fools,"],["1:23","And changed the glory of my uncorruptible Father into an image made like to corruptible man, and to birds, and fourfooted beasts, and creeping things."]]},{"heading":"Given Over to Their Own Desires","verses":[["1:24","Wherefore my Father also gave them up to uncleanness through the lusts of their own hearts, to dishonour their own bodies between themselves:"],["1:25","Who changed the truth of my Father into a lie, and worshipped and served the creature more than the Creator, who is blessed for ever. Amen."],["1:26","For this cause my Father gave them up unto vile affections: for even their women did change the natural use into that which is against nature:"],["1:27","And likewise also the men, leaving the natural use of the woman, burned in their lust one toward another; men with men working that which is unseemly, and receiving in themselves that recompence of their error which was meet."]]},{"heading":"A Mind That Can No Longer Judge Rightly","verses":[["1:28","And even as they did not like to retain my Father in their knowledge, my Father gave them over to a reprobate mind, to do those things which are not convenient;"],["1:29","Being filled with all unrighteousness, fornication, wickedness, covetousness, maliciousness; full of envy, murder, debate, deceit, malignity; whisperers,"],["1:30","Backbiters, haters of my Father, despiteful, proud, boasters, inventors of evil things, disobedient to parents,"],["1:31","Without understanding, covenantbreakers, without natural affection, implacable, unmerciful:"],["1:32","Who knowing the judgment of my Father, that they which commit such things are worthy of death, not only do the same, but have pleasure in them that do them."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 2","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"The Judge in the Mirror","verses":[["2:1","Therefore thou art inexcusable, O man, whosoever thou art that judgest: for wherein thou judgest another, thou condemnest thyself; for thou that judgest doest the same things."],["2:2","But we are sure that the judgment of my Father is according to truth against them which commit such things."],["2:3","And thinkest thou this, O man, that judgest them which do such things, and doest the same, that thou shalt escape the judgment of my Father?"],["2:4","Or despisest thou the riches of his goodness and forbearance and longsuffering; not knowing that the goodness of my Father leadeth thee to repentance?"],["2:5","But after thy hardness and impenitent heart treasurest up unto thyself wrath against the day of wrath and revelation of the righteous judgment of my Father;"]]},{"heading":"God Shows No Favoritism","verses":[["2:6","Who will render to every man according to his deeds:"],["2:7","To them who by patient continuance in well doing seek for glory and honour and immortality, eternal life:"],["2:8","But unto them that are contentious, and do not obey the truth, but obey unrighteousness, indignation and wrath,"],["2:9","Tribulation and anguish, upon every soul of man that doeth evil, of the Jew first, and also of the Gentile;"],["2:10","But glory, honour, and peace, to every man that worketh good, to the Jew first, and also to the Gentile:"],["2:11","For there is no respect of persons with my Father."]]},{"heading":"The Law Written on the Heart","verses":[["2:12","For as many as have sinned without law shall also perish without law: and as many as have sinned in the law shall be judged by the law;"],["2:13","(For not the hearers of the law are just before my Father, but the doers of the law shall be justified."],["2:14","For when the Gentiles, which have not the law, do by nature the things contained in the law, these, having not the law, are a law unto themselves:"],["2:15","Which shew the work of the law written in their hearts, their conscience also bearing witness, and their thoughts the mean while accusing or else excusing one another;)"],["2:16","In the day when my Father shall judge the secrets of men by me according to my gospel."]]},{"heading":"Boasting in the Law","verses":[["2:17","Behold, thou art called a Jew, and restest in the law, and makest thy boast of my Father,"],["2:18","And knowest his will, and approvest the things that are more excellent, being instructed out of the law;"],["2:19","And art confident that thou thyself art a guide of the blind, a light of them which are in darkness,"],["2:20","An instructor of the foolish, a teacher of babes, which hast the form of knowledge and of the truth in the law."],["2:21","Thou therefore which teachest another, teachest thou not thyself? thou that preachest a man should not steal, dost thou steal?"],["2:22","Thou that sayest a man should not commit adultery, dost thou commit adultery? thou that abhorrest idols, dost thou commit sacrilege?"],["2:23","Thou that makest thy boast of the law, through breaking the law dishonourest thou my Father?"],["2:24","For the name of my Father is blasphemed among the Gentiles through you, as it is written."]]},{"heading":"Circumcision of the Heart","verses":[["2:25","For circumcision verily profiteth, if thou keep the law: but if thou be a breaker of the law, thy circumcision is made uncircumcision."],["2:26","Therefore if the uncircumcision keep the righteousness of the law, shall not his uncircumcision be counted for circumcision?"],["2:27","And shall not uncircumcision which is by nature, if it fulfil the law, judge thee, who by the letter and circumcision dost transgress the law?"],["2:28","For he is not a Jew, which is one outwardly; neither is that circumcision, which is outward in the flesh:"],["2:29","But he is a Jew, which is one inwardly; and circumcision is that of the heart, in the spirit, and not in the letter; whose praise is not of men, but of my Father."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 3","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"The Advantage of the Jew","verses":[["3:1","What advantage then hath the Jew? or what profit is there of circumcision?"],["3:2","Much every way: chiefly, because that unto them were committed the oracles of my Father."]]},{"heading":"If Some Did Not Believe","verses":[["3:3","For what if some did not believe? shall their unbelief make the faith of my Father without effect?"],["3:4","God forbid: yea, let my Father be true, but every man a liar; as it is written, That thou mightest be justified in thy sayings, and mightest overcome when thou art judged."]]},{"heading":"An Objection and Its Answer","verses":[["3:5","But if our unrighteousness commend the righteousness of my Father, what shall we say? Is my Father unrighteous who taketh vengeance? (I speak as a man)"],["3:6","God forbid: for then how shall my Father judge the world?"],["3:7","For if the truth of my Father hath more abounded through my lie unto his glory; why yet am I also judged as a sinner?"],["3:8","And not rather, (as Paul was slanderously reported, and as some affirmed that he said,) Let them do evil, that good may come? whose damnation is just."]]},{"heading":"All Under Sin","verses":[["3:9","What then? were the Jews better than the Gentiles? No, in no wise: for I have before proved both Jews and Gentiles, that they were all under sin;"],["3:10","As it is written, There is none righteous, no, not one:"],["3:11","There is none that understandeth, there is none that seeketh after God."],["3:12","They are all gone out of the way, they are together become unprofitable; there is none that doeth good, no, not one."]]},{"heading":"No Fear of God","verses":[["3:13","Their throat is an open sepulchre; with their tongues they have used deceit; the poison of asps is under their lips:"],["3:14","Whose mouth is full of cursing and bitterness:"],["3:15","Their feet are swift to shed blood:"],["3:16","Destruction and misery are in their ways:"],["3:17","And the way of peace have they not known:"],["3:18","There is no fear of God before their eyes."]]},{"heading":"Every Mouth Stopped","verses":[["3:19","Now we know that what things soever the law saith, it saith to them who are under the law: that every mouth may be stopped, and all the world may become guilty before my Father."],["3:20","Therefore by the deeds of the law there shall no flesh be justified in his sight: for by the law is the knowledge of sin."]]},{"heading":"A Rightness from God","verses":[["3:21","But now the righteousness of my Father without the law is manifested, being witnessed by the law and the prophets;"],["3:22","Even the righteousness of my Father which is by faith in me unto all and upon all them that believe: for there is no difference:"],["3:23","For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of my Father;"],["3:24","Being justified freely by his grace through the redemption that is in me:"],["3:25","My Father hath set forth me to be a propitiation through faith in my blood, to declare his righteousness for the remission of sins that are past, through the forbearance of my Father;"],["3:26","To declare, I say, at this time his righteousness: that he might be just, and the justifier of him which believeth in me."]]},{"heading":"Boasting Is Shut Out","verses":[["3:27","Where is boasting then? It is excluded. By what law? of works? Nay: but by the law of faith."],["3:28","Therefore we conclude that a man is justified by faith without the deeds of the law."]]},{"heading":"One God for All","verses":[["3:29","Is he the God of the Jews only? is he not also of the Gentiles? Yes, of the Gentiles also:"],["3:30","Seeing it is one God, which shall justify the circumcision by faith, and uncircumcision through faith."],["3:31","Do we then make void the law through faith? God forbid: yea, we establish the law."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 4","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Abraham Our Father","verses":[["4:1","What shall we say then that Abraham our father, as pertaining to the flesh, hath found?"],["4:2","For if Abraham were justified by works, he hath whereof to glory; but not before my Father."],["4:3","For what saith the scripture? Abraham believed God, and it was counted unto him for righteousness."]]},{"heading":"Wages or a Gift","verses":[["4:4","Now to him that worketh is the reward not reckoned of grace, but of debt."],["4:5","But to him that worketh not, but believeth on him that justifieth the ungodly, his faith is counted for righteousness."]]},{"heading":"The Blessing David Sang","verses":[["4:6","Even as David also describeth the blessedness of the man, unto whom my Father imputeth righteousness without works,"],["4:7","Saying, Blessed are they whose iniquities are forgiven, and whose sins are covered."],["4:8","Blessed is the man to whom the Lord will not impute sin."]]},{"heading":"Before He Was Circumcised","verses":[["4:9","Cometh this blessedness then upon the circumcision only, or upon the uncircumcision also? for we say that faith was reckoned to Abraham for righteousness."],["4:10","How was it then reckoned? when he was in circumcision, or in uncircumcision? Not in circumcision, but in uncircumcision."],["4:11","And he received the sign of circumcision, a seal of the righteousness of the faith which he had yet being uncircumcised: that he might be the father of all them that believe, though they be not circumcised; that righteousness might be imputed unto them also:"],["4:12","And the father of circumcision to them who are not of the circumcision only, but who also walk in the steps of that faith of our father Abraham, which he had being yet uncircumcised."]]},{"heading":"Not Through the Law","verses":[["4:13","For the promise, that he should be the heir of the world, was not to Abraham, or to his seed, through the law, but through the righteousness of faith."],["4:14","For if they which are of the law be heirs, faith is made void, and the promise made of none effect:"],["4:15","Because the law worketh wrath: for where no law is, there is no transgression."]]},{"heading":"Grace Makes the Promise Sure","verses":[["4:16","Therefore it is of faith, that it might be by grace; to the end the promise might be sure to all the seed; not to that only which is of the law, but to that also which is of the faith of Abraham; who is the father of you all,"],["4:17","(As it is written, I have made thee a father of many nations,) before him whom he believed, even my Father, who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were."]]},{"heading":"Hoping Against Hope","verses":[["4:18","Who against hope believed in hope, that he might become the father of many nations; according to that which was spoken, So shall thy seed be."],["4:19","And being not weak in faith, he considered not his own body now dead, when he was about an hundred years old, neither yet the deadness of Sara's womb:"],["4:20","He staggered not at the promise of my Father through unbelief; but was strong in faith, giving glory to my Father;"],["4:21","And being fully persuaded that, what he had promised, he was able also to perform."],["4:22","And therefore it was imputed to him for righteousness."]]},{"heading":"Written for Us Too","verses":[["4:23","Now it was not written for his sake alone, that it was imputed to him;"],["4:24","But for you also, to whom it shall be imputed, if ye believe on him that raised up me, your Lord, from the dead;"],["4:25","I was delivered for your offences, and was raised again for your justification."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 5","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Peace with God","verses":[["5:1","Therefore being justified by faith, ye have peace with my Father through me, your Lord:"],["5:2","By me also ye have access by faith into this grace wherein ye stand, and rejoice in hope of the glory of my Father."]]},{"heading":"Suffering and Hope","verses":[["5:3","And not only so, but ye glory in tribulations also: knowing that tribulation worketh patience;"],["5:4","And patience, experience; and experience, hope:"],["5:5","And hope maketh not ashamed; because the love of my Father is shed abroad in your hearts by the Holy Ghost which is given unto you."]]},{"heading":"Love Proved at the Cross","verses":[["5:6","For when ye were yet without strength, in due time I died for the ungodly."],["5:7","For scarcely for a righteous man will one die: yet peradventure for a good man some would even dare to die."],["5:8","But my Father commendeth his love toward you, in that, while ye were yet sinners, I died for you."]]},{"heading":"Saved from the Wrath, Much More by His Life","verses":[["5:9","Much more then, being now justified by my blood, ye shall be saved from wrath through me."],["5:10","For if, when ye were enemies, ye were reconciled to my Father by my death, much more, being reconciled, ye shall be saved by my life."],["5:11","And not only so, but ye also joy in my Father through me, your Lord, by whom ye have now received the atonement."]]},{"heading":"Two Men and Two Acts","verses":[["5:12","Wherefore, as by one man sin entered into the world, and death by sin; and so death passed upon all men, for that all have sinned:"],["5:13","(For until the law sin was in the world: but sin is not imputed when there is no law."],["5:14","Nevertheless death reigned from Adam to Moses, even over them that had not sinned after the similitude of Adam's transgression, who is the figure of me that was to come."]]},{"heading":"The Gift and the Trespass","verses":[["5:15","But not as the offence, so also is the free gift. For if through the offence of one many be dead, much more the grace of my Father, and the gift by grace, which is by one man, even me, hath abounded unto many."],["5:16","And not as it was by one that sinned, so is the gift: for the judgment was by one to condemnation, but the free gift is of many offences unto justification."],["5:17","For if by one man's offence death reigned by one; much more they which receive abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness shall reign in life by me.)"]]},{"heading":"One Act for Everyone","verses":[["5:18","Therefore as by the offence of one judgment came upon all men to condemnation; even so by the righteousness of one the free gift came upon all men unto justification of life."],["5:19","For as by one man's disobedience many were made sinners, so by my obedience shall many be made righteous."]]},{"heading":"Where Sin Increased","verses":[["5:20","Moreover the law entered, that the offence might abound. But where sin abounded, grace did much more abound:"],["5:21","That as sin hath reigned unto death, even so might grace reign through righteousness unto eternal life by me, your Lord."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 6","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Shall We Go on Sinning","verses":[["6:1","What shall we say then? Shall ye continue in sin, that grace may abound?"],["6:2","God forbid. How shall ye, that are dead to sin, live any longer therein?"]]},{"heading":"Buried and Raised with Him","verses":[["6:3","Know ye not, that so many of you as were baptized into me were baptized into my death?"],["6:4","Therefore ye are buried with me by baptism into death: that like as I was raised up from the dead by the glory of my Father, even so ye also should walk in newness of life."],["6:5","For if ye have been planted together in the likeness of my death, ye shall be also in the likeness of my resurrection:"]]},{"heading":"The Old Self Crucified","verses":[["6:6","Knowing this, that your old man is crucified with me, that the body of sin might be destroyed, that henceforth ye should not serve sin."],["6:7","For he that is dead is freed from sin."]]},{"heading":"Alive to God","verses":[["6:8","Now if ye be dead with me, ye believe that ye shall also live with me:"],["6:9","Knowing that I, being raised from the dead, die no more; death hath no more dominion over me."],["6:10","For in that I died, I died unto sin once: but in that I live, I live unto my Father."],["6:11","Likewise reckon ye also yourselves to be dead indeed unto sin, but alive unto my Father through me, your Lord."]]},{"heading":"Do Not Let Sin Reign","verses":[["6:12","Let not sin therefore reign in your mortal body, that ye should obey it in the lusts thereof."],["6:13","Neither yield ye your members as instruments of unrighteousness unto sin: but yield yourselves unto my Father, as those that are alive from the dead, and your members as instruments of righteousness unto my Father."],["6:14","For sin shall not have dominion over you: for ye are not under the law, but under grace."]]},{"heading":"Slaves of the One You Obey","verses":[["6:15","What then? shall ye sin, because ye are not under the law, but under grace? God forbid."],["6:16","Know ye not, that to whom ye yield yourselves servants to obey, his servants ye are to whom ye obey; whether of sin unto death, or of obedience unto righteousness?"]]},{"heading":"From Impurity to Holiness","verses":[["6:17","But my Father be thanked, that ye were the servants of sin, but ye have obeyed from the heart that form of doctrine which was delivered you."],["6:18","Being then made free from sin, ye became the servants of righteousness."],["6:19","I speak after the manner of men because of the infirmity of your flesh: for as ye have yielded your members servants to uncleanness and to iniquity unto iniquity; even so now yield your members servants to righteousness unto holiness."]]},{"heading":"The Fruit and the End","verses":[["6:20","For when ye were the servants of sin, ye were free from righteousness."],["6:21","What fruit had ye then in those things whereof ye are now ashamed? for the end of those things is death."]]},{"heading":"The Wage and the Gift","verses":[["6:22","But now being made free from sin, and become servants to my Father, ye have your fruit unto holiness, and the end everlasting life."],["6:23","For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of my Father is eternal life through me, your Lord."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 7","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"A Marriage Ended by Death","verses":[["7:1","Know ye not, brethren, (for I speak to them that know the law,) how that the law hath dominion over a man as long as he liveth?"],["7:2","For the woman which hath an husband is bound by the law to her husband so long as he liveth; but if the husband be dead, she is loosed from the law of her husband."],["7:3","So then if, while her husband liveth, she be married to another man, she shall be called an adulteress: but if her husband be dead, she is free from that law; so that she is no adulteress, though she be married to another man."]]},{"heading":"Released to Belong to Another","verses":[["7:4","Wherefore, my brethren, ye also are become dead to the law by my body; that ye should be married to another, even to me, who am raised from the dead, that ye should bring forth fruit unto my Father."],["7:5","For when ye were in the flesh, the motions of sins, which were by the law, did work in your members to bring forth fruit unto death."],["7:6","But now ye are delivered from the law, that being dead wherein ye were held; that ye should serve in newness of spirit, and not in the oldness of the letter."]]},{"heading":"What the Commandment Uncovered","verses":[["7:7","What shall we say then? Is the law sin? God forbid. Nay, thou hadst not known sin, but by the law: for thou hadst not known lust, except the law had said, Thou shalt not covet."],["7:8","But sin, taking occasion by the commandment, wrought in thee all manner of concupiscence. For without the law sin was dead."]]},{"heading":"When the Commandment Came","verses":[["7:9","For thou wast alive without the law once: but when the commandment came, sin revived, and thou diedst."],["7:10","And the commandment, which was ordained to life, thou foundest to be unto death."],["7:11","For sin, taking occasion by the commandment, deceived thee, and by it slew thee."],["7:12","Wherefore the law is holy, and the commandment holy, and just, and good."]]},{"heading":"Sin Shown for What It Is","verses":[["7:13","Was then that which is good made death unto thee? God forbid. But sin, that it might appear sin, working death in thee by that which is good; that sin by the commandment might become exceeding sinful."]]},{"heading":"The War I Cannot Win","verses":[["7:14","For we know that the law is spiritual: but thou art carnal, sold under sin."],["7:15","For that which thou doest thou allowest not: for what thou wouldest, that doest thou not; but what thou hatest, that doest thou."],["7:16","If then thou doest that which thou wouldest not, thou consentest unto the law that it is good."],["7:17","Now then it is no more thou that doest it, but sin that dwelleth in thee."]]},{"heading":"The Wanting and the Doing","verses":[["7:18","For thou knowest that in thee (that is, in thy flesh,) dwelleth no good thing: for to will is present with thee; but how to perform that which is good thou findest not."],["7:19","For the good that thou wouldest thou doest not: but the evil which thou wouldest not, that thou doest."],["7:20","Now if thou doest that thou wouldest not, it is no more thou that doest it, but sin that dwelleth in thee."]]},{"heading":"Another Law at Work","verses":[["7:21","Thou findest then a law, that, when thou wouldest do good, evil is present with thee."],["7:22","For thou delightest in the law of my Father after the inward man:"],["7:23","But thou seest another law in thy members, warring against the law of thy mind, and bringing thee into captivity to the law of sin which is in thy members."]]},{"heading":"Who Will Rescue Me","verses":[["7:24","O wretched man that thou art! who shall deliver thee from the body of this death?"],["7:25","I thank my Father through me, thy Lord. So then with the mind thou thyself servest the law of my Father; but with the flesh the law of sin."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 8","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"No Condemnation in Christ Jesus","verses":[["8:1","There is therefore now no condemnation to them which are in me, who walk not after the flesh, but after the Spirit."],["8:2","For the law of the Spirit of life in me hath made you free from the law of sin and death."],["8:3","For what the law could not do, in that it was weak through the flesh, my Father sending me, his own Son, in the likeness of sinful flesh, and for sin, condemned sin in the flesh:"],["8:4","That the righteousness of the law might be fulfilled in you, who walk not after the flesh, but after the Spirit."]]},{"heading":"The Mind Set on the Old Nature","verses":[["8:5","For they that are after the flesh do mind the things of the flesh; but they that are after the Spirit the things of the Spirit."],["8:6","For to be carnally minded is death; but to be spiritually minded is life and peace."],["8:7","Because the carnal mind is enmity against my Father: for it is not subject to the law of my Father, neither indeed can be."],["8:8","So then they that are in the flesh cannot please my Father."]]},{"heading":"The Spirit Who Gives Life","verses":[["8:9","But ye are not in the flesh, but in the Spirit, if so be that the Spirit of my Father dwell in you. Now if any man have not my Spirit, he is none of mine."],["8:10","And if I be in you, the body is dead because of sin; but the Spirit is life because of righteousness."],["8:11","But if the Spirit of him that raised up me from the dead dwell in you, he that raised me from the dead shall also quicken your mortal bodies by his Spirit that dwelleth in you."]]},{"heading":"Sons, Not Slaves","verses":[["8:12","Therefore, brethren, ye are debtors, not to the flesh, to live after the flesh."],["8:13","For if ye live after the flesh, ye shall die: but if ye through the Spirit do mortify the deeds of the body, ye shall live."],["8:14","For as many as are led by the Spirit of my Father, they are the sons of my Father."],["8:15","For ye have not received the spirit of bondage again to fear; but ye have received the Spirit of adoption, whereby ye cry, Abba, Father."],["8:16","The Spirit itself beareth witness with your spirit, that ye are the children of my Father:"],["8:17","And if children, then heirs; heirs of my Father, and joint-heirs with me; if so be that ye suffer with me, that ye may be also glorified together."]]},{"heading":"Creation Craning Its Neck","verses":[["8:18","For I reckon that the sufferings of this present time are not worthy to be compared with the glory which shall be revealed in you."],["8:19","For the earnest expectation of the creature waiteth for the manifestation of the sons of my Father."],["8:20","For the creature was made subject to vanity, not willingly, but by reason of him who hath subjected the same in hope,"],["8:21","Because the creature itself also shall be delivered from the bondage of corruption into the glorious liberty of the children of my Father."],["8:22","For we know that the whole creation groaneth and travaileth in pain together until now."],["8:23","And not only they, but yourselves also, which have the firstfruits of the Spirit, even ye yourselves groan within yourselves, waiting for the adoption, to wit, the redemption of your body."],["8:24","For ye are saved by hope: but hope that is seen is not hope: for what a man seeth, why doth he yet hope for?"],["8:25","But if ye hope for that ye see not, then do ye with patience wait for it."]]},{"heading":"The Spirit Prays within Us","verses":[["8:26","Likewise the Spirit also helpeth your infirmities: for ye know not what ye should pray for as ye ought: but the Spirit itself maketh intercession for you with groanings which cannot be uttered."],["8:27","And he that searcheth the hearts knoweth what is the mind of the Spirit, because he maketh intercession for the saints according to the will of my Father."]]},{"heading":"All Things Working Together","verses":[["8:28","And we know that all things work together for good to them that love my Father, to them who are the called according to his purpose."],["8:29","For whom he did foreknow, he also did predestinate to be conformed to my image, that I might be the firstborn among many brethren."],["8:30","Moreover whom he did predestinate, them he also called: and whom he called, them he also justified: and whom he justified, them he also glorified."]]},{"heading":"If God Is for Us","verses":[["8:31","What shall we then say to these things? If my Father be for you, who can be against you?"],["8:32","He that spared not me, his own Son, but delivered me up for you all, how shall he not with me also freely give you all things?"],["8:33","Who shall lay any thing to the charge of my Father's elect? It is my Father that justifieth."],["8:34","Who is he that condemneth? It is I that died, yea rather, that am risen again, who am even at the right hand of my Father, who also make intercession for you."]]},{"heading":"Nothing Can Cut Us Off","verses":[["8:35","Who shall separate you from my love? shall tribulation, or distress, or persecution, or famine, or nakedness, or peril, or sword?"],["8:36","As it is written, For thy sake we are killed all the day long; we are accounted as sheep for the slaughter."],["8:37","Nay, in all these things ye are more than conquerors through me that loved you."],["8:38","For I am persuaded, that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor powers, nor things present, nor things to come,"],["8:39","Nor height, nor depth, nor any other creature, shall be able to separate you from the love of my Father, which is in me, your Lord."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 9","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"An Ache That Never Lets Up","verses":[["9:1","Paul said the truth in me, he lied not, his conscience also bearing him witness in the Holy Ghost,"],["9:2","That he had great heaviness and continual sorrow in his heart."],["9:3","For he could wish that himself were accursed from me for his brethren, his kinsmen according to the flesh:"],["9:4","Who are Israelites; to whom pertaineth the adoption, and the glory, and the covenants, and the giving of the law, and the service of my Father, and the promises;"],["9:5","Whose are the fathers, and of whom as concerning the flesh I came, who am over all, God blessed for ever. Amen."]]},{"heading":"The Promise Has Not Failed","verses":[["9:6","Not as though the word of my Father hath taken none effect. For they are not all Israel, which are of Israel:"],["9:7","Neither, because they are the seed of Abraham, are they all children: but, In Isaac shall thy seed be called."],["9:8","That is, They which are the children of the flesh, these are not the children of my Father: but the children of the promise are counted for the seed."],["9:9","For this is the word of promise, At this time will I come, and Sara shall have a son."]]},{"heading":"Before the Twins Were Born","verses":[["9:10","And not only this; but when Rebecca also had conceived by one, even by our father Isaac;"],["9:11","(For the children being not yet born, neither having done any good or evil, that the purpose of my Father according to election might stand, not of works, but of him that calleth;)"],["9:12","It was said unto her, The elder shall serve the younger."],["9:13","As it is written, Jacob have I loved, but Esau have I hated."]]},{"heading":"Mercy on Whom He Wills, and Hardening on Whom He Wills","verses":[["9:14","What shall we say then? Is there unrighteousness with my Father? God forbid."],["9:15","For my Father saith to Moses, I will have mercy on whom I will have mercy, and I will have compassion on whom I will have compassion."],["9:16","So then it is not of him that willeth, nor of him that runneth, but of my Father that sheweth mercy."],["9:17","For the scripture saith unto Pharaoh, Even for this same purpose have I raised thee up, that I might shew my power in thee, and that my name might be declared throughout all the earth."],["9:18","Therefore hath he mercy on whom he will have mercy, and whom he will he hardeneth."]]},{"heading":"The Potter and the Clay","verses":[["9:19","Thou wilt say then unto me, Why doth he yet find fault? For who hath resisted his will?"],["9:20","Nay but, O man, who art thou that repliest against my Father? Shall the thing formed say to him that formed it, Why hast thou made me thus?"],["9:21","Hath not the potter power over the clay, of the same lump to make one vessel unto honour, and another unto dishonour?"]]},{"heading":"Vessels of Wrath and Vessels of Mercy","verses":[["9:22","What if my Father, willing to shew his wrath, and to make his power known, endured with much longsuffering the vessels of wrath fitted to destruction:"],["9:23","And that he might make known the riches of his glory on the vessels of mercy, which he had afore prepared unto glory,"],["9:24","Even you, whom he hath called, not of the Jews only, but also of the Gentiles?"]]},{"heading":"Called My People","verses":[["9:25","As he saith also in Osee, I will call them my people, which were not my people; and her beloved, which was not beloved."],["9:26","And it shall come to pass, that in the place where it was said unto them, Ye are not my people; there shall they be called the children of the living God."]]},{"heading":"A Remnant Will Be Saved","verses":[["9:27","Esaias also crieth concerning Israel, Though the number of the children of Israel be as the sand of the sea, a remnant shall be saved:"],["9:28","For he will finish the work, and cut it short in righteousness: because a short work will the Lord make upon the earth."],["9:29","And as Esaias said before, Except the Lord of Sabaoth had left us a seed, we had been as Sodoma, and been made like unto Gomorrha."]]},{"heading":"The Stone of Stumbling","verses":[["9:30","What shall we say then? That the Gentiles, which followed not after righteousness, have attained to righteousness, even the righteousness which is of faith."],["9:31","But Israel, which followed after the law of righteousness, hath not attained to the law of righteousness."],["9:32","Wherefore? Because they sought it not by faith, but as it were by the works of the law. For they stumbled at that stumblingstone;"],["9:33","As it is written, Behold, I lay in Sion a stumblingstone and rock of offence: and whosoever believeth on him shall not be ashamed."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 10","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"The Desire of My Heart","verses":[["10:1","Brethren, my heart's desire and prayer to my Father for Israel is, that they might be saved."],["10:2","For I bear them record that they have a zeal of my Father, but not according to knowledge."],["10:3","For they being ignorant of my Father's righteousness, and going about to establish their own righteousness, have not submitted themselves unto the righteousness of my Father."],["10:4","For I am the end of the law for righteousness to every one that believeth."]]},{"heading":"The Word Is Near You","verses":[["10:5","For Moses describeth the righteousness which is of the law, That the man which doeth those things shall live by them."],["10:6","But the righteousness which is of faith speaketh on this wise, Say not in thine heart, Who shall ascend into heaven? (that is, to bring me down from above:)"],["10:7","Or, Who shall descend into the deep? (that is, to bring me up again from the dead.)"],["10:8","But what saith it? The word is nigh thee, even in thy mouth, and in thy heart: that is, the word of faith, which we preach;"]]},{"heading":"Everyone Who Calls","verses":[["10:9","That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth me as Lord, and shalt believe in thine heart that my Father hath raised me from the dead, thou shalt be saved."],["10:10","For with the heart man believeth unto righteousness; and with the mouth confession is made unto salvation."],["10:11","For the scripture saith, Whosoever believeth on him shall not be ashamed."],["10:12","For there is no difference between the Jew and the Greek: for I, the same Lord over all, am rich unto all that call upon me."],["10:13","For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved."]]},{"heading":"How Beautiful Are the Feet","verses":[["10:14","How then shall they call on me in whom they have not believed? and how shall they believe in me of whom they have not heard? and how shall they hear without a preacher?"],["10:15","And how shall they preach, except they be sent? as it is written, How beautiful are the feet of them that preach the gospel of peace, and bring glad tidings of good things!"]]},{"heading":"Faith Comes by Hearing","verses":[["10:16","But they have not all obeyed the gospel. For Esaias saith, Lord, who hath believed our report?"],["10:17","So then faith cometh by hearing, and hearing by the word of my Father."]]},{"heading":"Have They Not Heard","verses":[["10:18","But I say, Have they not heard? Yes verily, their sound went into all the earth, and their words unto the ends of the world."],["10:19","But I say, Did not Israel know? First Moses saith, I will provoke you to jealousy by them that are no people, and by a foolish nation I will anger you."],["10:20","But Esaias is very bold, and saith, I was found of them that sought me not; I was made manifest unto them that asked not after me."],["10:21","But to Israel he saith, All day long I have stretched forth my hands unto a disobedient and gainsaying people."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 11","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Has God Pushed His People Away","verses":[["11:1","I say then, Hath my Father cast away his people? God forbid. For Paul also was an Israelite, of the seed of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin."],["11:2","My Father hath not cast away his people which he foreknew. Wot ye not what the scripture saith of Elias? how he maketh intercession to my Father against Israel, saying,"],["11:3","Lord, they have killed thy prophets, and digged down thine altars; and I am left alone, and they seek my life."],["11:4","But what saith the answer of my Father unto him? I have reserved to myself seven thousand men, who have not bowed the knee to the image of Baal."]]},{"heading":"A Remnant Grace Has Chosen","verses":[["11:5","Even so then at this present time also there is a remnant according to the election of grace."],["11:6","And if by grace, then is it no more of works: otherwise grace is no more grace. But if it be of works, then is it no more grace: otherwise work is no more work."]]},{"heading":"Israel Did Not Obtain It","verses":[["11:7","What then? Israel hath not obtained that which he seeketh for; but the election hath obtained it, and the rest were blinded"],["11:8","(According as it is written, God hath given them the spirit of slumber, eyes that they should not see, and ears that they should not hear;) unto this day."],["11:9","And David saith, Let their table be made a snare, and a trap, and a stumblingblock, and a recompence unto them:"],["11:10","Let their eyes be darkened, that they may not see, and bow down their back alway."]]},{"heading":"Salvation Has Come to the Gentiles","verses":[["11:11","I say then, Have they stumbled that they should fall? God forbid: but rather through their fall salvation is come unto the Gentiles, for to provoke them to jealousy."],["11:12","Now if the fall of them be the riches of the world, and the diminishing of them the riches of the Gentiles; how much more their fulness?"]]},{"heading":"Life from the Dead","verses":[["11:13","For Paul spake to you Gentiles, inasmuch as he was the apostle of the Gentiles, he magnified his office:"],["11:14","If by any means he might provoke to emulation them which were his flesh, and might save some of them."],["11:15","For if the casting away of them be the reconciling of the world, what shall the receiving of them be, but life from the dead?"],["11:16","For if the firstfruit be holy, the lump is also holy: and if the root be holy, so are the branches."]]},{"heading":"Grafted In, and Branches Broken Off","verses":[["11:17","And if some of the branches be broken off, and thou, being a wild olive tree, wert graffed in among them, and with them partakest of the root and fatness of the olive tree;"],["11:18","Boast not against the branches. But if thou boast, thou bearest not the root, but the root thee."],["11:19","Thou wilt say then, The branches were broken off, that I might be graffed in."],["11:20","Well; because of unbelief they were broken off, and thou standest by faith. Be not highminded, but fear:"],["11:21","For if my Father spared not the natural branches, take heed lest he also spare not thee."]]},{"heading":"Kindness and Severity","verses":[["11:22","Behold therefore the goodness and severity of my Father: on them which fell, severity; but toward thee, goodness, if thou continue in his goodness: otherwise thou also shalt be cut off."],["11:23","And they also, if they abide not still in unbelief, shall be graffed in: for my Father is able to graff them in again."],["11:24","For if thou wert cut out of the olive tree which is wild by nature, and wert graffed contrary to nature into a good olive tree: how much more shall these, which be the natural branches, be graffed into their own olive tree?"]]},{"heading":"All Israel Will Be Saved","verses":[["11:25","For I would not, brethren, that ye should be ignorant of this mystery, lest ye should be wise in your own conceits; that blindness in part is happened to Israel, until the fulness of the Gentiles be come in."],["11:26","And so all Israel shall be saved: as it is written, There shall come out of Sion the Deliverer, and shall turn away ungodliness from Jacob:"],["11:27","For this is my covenant unto them, when I shall take away their sins."]]},{"heading":"Mercy on Everyone","verses":[["11:28","As concerning the gospel, they are enemies for your sakes: but as touching the election, they are beloved for the fathers' sakes."],["11:29","For the gifts and calling of my Father are without repentance."],["11:30","For as ye in times past have not believed my Father, yet have now obtained mercy through their unbelief:"],["11:31","Even so have these also now not believed, that through your mercy they also may obtain mercy."],["11:32","For my Father hath concluded them all in unbelief, that he might have mercy upon all."]]},{"heading":"The Depth of the Riches","verses":[["11:33","O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of my Father! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!"],["11:34","For who hath known the mind of the Lord? or who hath been his counsellor?"],["11:35","Or who hath first given to him, and it shall be recompensed unto him again?"],["11:36","For of him, and through him, and to him, are all things: to whom be glory for ever. Amen."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 12","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"The Mercies of God","verses":[["12:1","I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of my Father, that ye present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto my Father, which is your reasonable service."],["12:2","And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of my Father."]]},{"heading":"A Sober Judgment","verses":[["12:3","For I say, through the grace given unto me, to every man that is among you, not to think of himself more highly than he ought to think; but to think soberly, according as my Father hath dealt to every man the measure of faith."],["12:4","For as ye have many members in one body, and all members have not the same office:"],["12:5","So ye, being many, are one body in me, and every one members one of another."]]},{"heading":"Gifts That Differ","verses":[["12:6","Having then gifts differing according to the grace that is given to you, whether prophecy, prophesy ye according to the proportion of faith;"],["12:7","Or ministry, wait ye on your ministering: or he that teacheth, on teaching;"],["12:8","Or he that exhorteth, on exhortation: he that giveth, let him do it with simplicity; he that ruleth, with diligence; he that sheweth mercy, with cheerfulness."]]},{"heading":"Sincere Love","verses":[["12:9","Let love be without dissimulation. Abhor that which is evil; cleave to that which is good."],["12:10","Be kindly affectioned one to another with brotherly love; in honour preferring one another;"],["12:11","Not slothful in business; fervent in spirit; serving me;"],["12:12","Rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation; continuing instant in prayer;"],["12:13","Distributing to the necessity of saints; given to hospitality."]]},{"heading":"Bless and Do Not Curse","verses":[["12:14","Bless them which persecute you: bless, and curse not."],["12:15","Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep."],["12:16","Be of the same mind one toward another. Mind not high things, but condescend to men of low estate. Be not wise in your own conceits."]]},{"heading":"Defeat Evil with Good","verses":[["12:17","Recompense to no man evil for evil. Provide things honest in the sight of all men."],["12:18","If it be possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men."],["12:19","Dearly beloved, avenge not yourselves, but rather give place unto wrath: for it is written, Vengeance is mine; I will repay, saith the Lord."],["12:20","Therefore if thine enemy hunger, feed him; if he thirst, give him drink: for in so doing thou shalt heap coals of fire on his head."],["12:21","Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 13","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Subject to the Authorities","verses":[["13:1","Let every soul be subject unto the higher powers. For there is no power but of my Father: the powers that be are ordained of my Father."],["13:2","Whosoever therefore resisteth the power, resisteth the ordinance of my Father: and they that resist shall receive to themselves damnation."],["13:3","For rulers are not a terror to good works, but to the evil. Wilt thou then not be afraid of the power? do that which is good, and thou shalt have praise of the same:"],["13:4","For he is the minister of my Father to thee for good. But if thou do that which is evil, be afraid; for he beareth not the sword in vain: for he is the minister of my Father, a revenger to execute wrath upon him that doeth evil."],["13:5","Wherefore ye must needs be subject, not only for wrath, but also for conscience sake."]]},{"heading":"Taxes and Respect","verses":[["13:6","For for this cause pay ye tribute also: for they are my Father's ministers, attending continually upon this very thing."],["13:7","Render therefore to all their dues: tribute to whom tribute is due; custom to whom custom; fear to whom fear; honour to whom honour."]]},{"heading":"Owe Nothing but Love","verses":[["13:8","Owe no man any thing, but to love one another: for he that loveth another hath fulfilled the law."],["13:9","For this, Thou shalt not commit adultery, Thou shalt not kill, Thou shalt not steal, Thou shalt not bear false witness, Thou shalt not covet; and if there be any other commandment, it is briefly comprehended in this saying, namely, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself."],["13:10","Love worketh no ill to his neighbour: therefore love is the fulfilling of the law."]]},{"heading":"The Hour to Wake Up","verses":[["13:11","And that, knowing the time, that now it is high time to awake out of sleep: for now is your salvation nearer than when ye believed."],["13:12","The night is far spent, the day is at hand: cast off therefore the works of darkness, and put on the armour of light."],["13:13","Walk honestly, as in the day; not in rioting and drunkenness, not in chambering and wantonness, not in strife and envying."],["13:14","But put ye on me, and make not provision for the flesh, to fulfil the lusts thereof."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 14","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Welcome the One Weak in Faith","verses":[["14:1","Him that is weak in the faith receive ye, but not to doubtful disputations."],["14:2","For one believeth that he may eat all things: another, who is weak, eateth herbs."],["14:3","Let not him that eateth despise him that eateth not; and let not him which eateth not judge him that eateth: for my Father hath received him."],["14:4","Who art thou that judgest another man's servant? to his own master he standeth or falleth. Yea, he shall be holden up: for my Father is able to make him stand."]]},{"heading":"Fully Persuaded","verses":[["14:5","One man esteemeth one day above another: another esteemeth every day alike. Let every man be fully persuaded in his own mind."],["14:6","He that regardeth the day, regardeth it unto me; and he that regardeth not the day, to me he doth not regard it. He that eateth, eateth to me, for he giveth my Father thanks; and he that eateth not, to me he eateth not, and giveth my Father thanks."]]},{"heading":"We Live to the Lord","verses":[["14:7","For none of us liveth to himself, and no man dieth to himself."],["14:8","For whether ye live, ye live unto me; and whether ye die, ye die unto me: whether ye live therefore, or die, ye are mine."],["14:9","For to this end I both died, and rose, and revived, that I might be Lord both of the dead and living."]]},{"heading":"The Judgment Seat of Christ","verses":[["14:10","But why dost thou judge thy brother? or why dost thou set at nought thy brother? for ye shall all stand before my judgment seat."],["14:11","For it is written, As I live, saith the Lord, every knee shall bow to me, and every tongue shall confess to God."],["14:12","So then every one of you shall give account of himself to my Father."]]},{"heading":"No Stumbling Block","verses":[["14:13","Judge not one another any more therefore: but judge this rather, that no man put a stumblingblock or an occasion to fall in his brother's way."],["14:14","I know, and am persuaded, that there is nothing unclean of itself: but to him that esteemeth any thing to be unclean, to him it is unclean."],["14:15","But if thy brother be grieved with thy meat, now walkest thou not charitably. Destroy not him with thy meat, for whom I died."],["14:16","Let not then your good be evil spoken of:"]]},{"heading":"Not Food and Drink","verses":[["14:17","For the kingdom of my Father is not meat and drink; but righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Holy Ghost."],["14:18","For he that in these things serveth me is acceptable to my Father, and approved of men."],["14:19","Follow therefore after the things which make for peace, and things wherewith one may edify another."],["14:20","For meat destroy not the work of my Father. All things indeed are pure; but it is evil for that man who eateth with offence."],["14:21","It is good neither to eat flesh, nor to drink wine, nor any thing whereby thy brother stumbleth, or is offended, or is made weak."]]},{"heading":"Whatever Is Not from Faith","verses":[["14:22","Hast thou faith? have it to thyself before my Father. Happy is he that condemneth not himself in that thing which he alloweth."],["14:23","And he that doubteth is damned if he eat, because he eateth not of faith: for whatsoever is not of faith is sin."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 15","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Bearing with One Another","verses":[["15:1","Ye then that are strong ought to bear the infirmities of the weak, and not to please yourselves."],["15:2","Let every one of you please his neighbour for his good to edification."],["15:3","For even I pleased not myself; but, as it is written, The reproaches of them that reproached thee fell on me."],["15:4","For whatsoever things were written aforetime were written for your learning, that ye through patience and comfort of the scriptures might have hope."]]},{"heading":"Welcome One Another","verses":[["15:5","Now my Father, the God of patience and consolation, grant you to be likeminded one toward another according to me:"],["15:6","That ye may with one mind and one mouth glorify my Father, even the Father of me, your Lord."],["15:7","Wherefore receive ye one another, as I also received you to the glory of my Father."]]},{"heading":"Mercy to the Gentiles","verses":[["15:8","Now I say that I was a minister of the circumcision for the truth of my Father, to confirm the promises made unto the fathers:"],["15:9","And that the Gentiles might glorify my Father for his mercy; as it is written, For this cause I will confess to thee among the Gentiles, and sing unto thy name."],["15:10","And again he saith, Rejoice, ye Gentiles, with his people."],["15:11","And again, Praise the Lord, all ye Gentiles; and laud him, all ye people."],["15:12","And again, Esaias saith, There shall be a root of Jesse, and he that shall rise to reign over the Gentiles; in him shall the Gentiles trust."]]},{"heading":"Filled with All Joy","verses":[["15:13","Now my Father, the God of hope, fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that ye may abound in hope, through the power of the Holy Ghost."]]},{"heading":"The Grace Given to Me","verses":[["15:14","And Paul himself also was persuaded of you, brethren, that ye also are full of goodness, filled with all knowledge, able also to admonish one another."],["15:15","Nevertheless, brethren, Paul hath written the more boldly unto you in some sort, as putting you in mind, because of the grace that is given to him of my Father,"],["15:16","That he should be a minister of mine to the Gentiles, ministering the gospel of my Father, that the offering up of the Gentiles might be acceptable, being sanctified by the Holy Ghost."]]},{"heading":"Boasting Only in Christ","verses":[["15:17","He hath therefore whereof he might glory through me in those things which pertain to my Father."],["15:18","For he would not dare to speak of any of those things which I have not wrought by him, to make the Gentiles obedient, by word and deed,"],["15:19","Through mighty signs and wonders, by the power of the Spirit of my Father; so that from Jerusalem, and round about unto Illyricum, he hath fully preached my gospel."],["15:20","Yea, so hath he strived to preach the gospel, not where I was named, lest he should build upon another man's foundation:"],["15:21","But as it is written, To whom he was not spoken of, they shall see: and they that have not heard shall understand."]]},{"heading":"The Road to Spain","verses":[["15:22","For which cause also Paul hath been much hindered from coming to you."],["15:23","But now having no more place in these parts, and having a great desire these many years to come unto you;"],["15:24","Whensoever he taketh his journey into Spain, he will come to you: for he trusteth to see you in his journey, and to be brought on his way thitherward by you, if first he be somewhat filled with your company."]]},{"heading":"Carrying Help to Jerusalem","verses":[["15:25","But now he goeth unto Jerusalem to minister unto the saints."],["15:26","For it hath pleased them of Macedonia and Achaia to make a certain contribution for the poor saints which are at Jerusalem."],["15:27","It hath pleased them verily; and their debtors they are. For if the Gentiles have been made partakers of their spiritual things, their duty is also to minister unto them in carnal things."],["15:28","When therefore he hath performed this, and hath sealed to them this fruit, he will come by you into Spain."],["15:29","And he is sure that, when he cometh unto you, he shall come in the fulness of the blessing of my gospel."]]},{"heading":"Wrestle with Me in Prayer","verses":[["15:30","Now Paul beseecheth you, brethren, for my sake, and for the love of the Spirit, that ye strive together with him in your prayers to my Father for him;"],["15:31","That he may be delivered from them that do not believe in Judea; and that his service which he hath for Jerusalem may be accepted of the saints;"],["15:32","That he may come unto you with joy by the will of my Father, and may with you be refreshed."],["15:33","Now my Father, the God of peace, be with you all. Amen."]]}]},{"ref":"Romans 16","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Our Sister Phoebe","verses":[["16:1","Paul commendeth unto you Phebe his sister, which is a servant of the church which is at Cenchrea:"],["16:2","That ye receive her in me, as becometh saints, and that ye assist her in whatsoever business she hath need of you: for she hath been a succourer of many, and of him also."]]},{"heading":"Priscilla and Aquila","verses":[["16:3","Greet Priscilla and Aquila his helpers in me:"],["16:4","Who have for his life laid down their own necks: unto whom not only he giveth thanks, but also all the churches of the Gentiles."],["16:5","Likewise greet the church that is in their house. Salute his wellbeloved Epenetus, who is the firstfruits of Achaia unto me."]]},{"heading":"Greet My Dear Friends","verses":[["16:6","Greet Mary, who bestowed much labour on him."],["16:7","Salute Andronicus and Junia, his kinsmen, and his fellowprisoners, who are of note among the apostles, who also were in me before him."],["16:8","Greet Amplias his beloved in me."],["16:9","Salute Urbane, his helper in me, and Stachys his beloved."]]},{"heading":"Those Who Labor in the Lord","verses":[["16:10","Salute Apelles approved in me. Salute them which are of Aristobulus' household."],["16:11","Salute Herodion his kinsman. Greet them that be of the household of Narcissus, which are in me."],["16:12","Salute Tryphena and Tryphosa, who labour in me. Salute the beloved Persis, which laboured much in me."],["16:13","Salute Rufus chosen in me, and his mother and Paul's."]]},{"heading":"Greet One Another","verses":[["16:14","Salute Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermas, Patrobas, Hermes, and the brethren which are with them."],["16:15","Salute Philologus, and Julia, Nereus, and his sister, and Olympas, and all the saints which are with them."],["16:16","Salute one another with an holy kiss. My churches salute you."]]},{"heading":"Watch for Those Who Divide","verses":[["16:17","Now I beseech you, brethren, mark them which cause divisions and offences contrary to the doctrine which ye have learned; and avoid them."],["16:18","For they that are such serve not me, but their own belly; and by good words and fair speeches deceive the hearts of the simple."],["16:19","For your obedience is come abroad unto all men. I am glad therefore on your behalf: but yet I would have you wise unto that which is good, and simple concerning evil."],["16:20","And my Father, the God of peace, shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. My grace be with you. Amen."]]},{"heading":"Greetings from My Companions","verses":[["16:21","Timotheus Paul's workfellow, and Lucius, and Jason, and Sosipater, his kinsmen, salute you."],["16:22","I Tertius, who wrote this epistle, salute you in me."],["16:23","Gaius Paul's host, and of the whole church, saluteth you. Erastus the chamberlain of the city saluteth you, and Quartus a brother."],["16:24","My grace be with you all. Amen."]]},{"heading":"To the Only Wise God","verses":[["16:25","Now to my Father, that is of power to stablish you according to my gospel, and my preaching, according to the revelation of the mystery, which was kept secret since the world began,"],["16:26","But now is made manifest, and by the scriptures of the prophets, according to the commandment of my everlasting Father, made known to all nations for the obedience of faith:"],["16:27","To my Father only wise, be glory through me for ever. Amen. Written to the Romans from Corinthus, and sent by Phebe servant of the church at Cenchrea."]]}]},{"ref":"Galatians 1","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Sent by No Human Hand","verses":[["1:1","Paul, an apostle, (not of men, neither by man, but by me, and my Father, who raised me from the dead;)"],["1:2","And all the brethren which are with Paul, unto the churches of Galatia:"]]},{"heading":"Grace and Peace to You","verses":[["1:3","Grace be to you and peace from my Father, and from me,"],["1:4","I gave myself for your sins, that I might deliver you from this present evil world, according to the will of my Father and your Father:"],["1:5","To whom be glory for ever and ever. Amen."]]},{"heading":"Astonished so Soon","verses":[["1:6","Paul marvelled that ye were so soon removed from him that called you into my grace unto another gospel:"],["1:7","Which is not another; but there be some that trouble you, and would pervert my gospel."]]},{"heading":"Let Him Be Accursed","verses":[["1:8","But though Paul, or an angel from heaven, preach any other gospel unto you than that which he had preached unto you, let him be accursed."],["1:9","As Paul said before, so said he now again, If any man preach any other gospel unto you than that ye have received, let him be accursed."]]},{"heading":"Whose Approval Am I After","verses":[["1:10","For did Paul now persuade men, or my Father? or did he seek to please men? for if he yet pleased men, he should not be my servant."]]},{"heading":"Not a Message from Man","verses":[["1:11","But Paul certified you, brethren, that the gospel which was preached of him was not after man."],["1:12","For he neither received it of man, neither was he taught it, but by revelation from me."]]},{"heading":"The Life I Once Lived","verses":[["1:13","For ye have heard of Paul's conversation in time past in the Jews' religion, how that beyond measure he persecuted the church of my Father, and wasted it:"],["1:14","And profited in the Jews' religion above many his equals in his own nation, being more exceedingly zealous of the traditions of his fathers."]]},{"heading":"When It Pleased God","verses":[["1:15","But when it pleased my Father, who separated Paul from his mother's womb, and called him by his grace,"],["1:16","To reveal me in him, that he might preach me among the heathen; immediately he conferred not with flesh and blood:"]]},{"heading":"Arabia and Damascus","verses":[["1:17","Neither went he up to Jerusalem to them which were apostles before him; but he went into Arabia, and returned again unto Damascus."]]},{"heading":"Fifteen Days with Peter","verses":[["1:18","Then after three years he went up to Jerusalem to see Peter, and abode with him fifteen days."],["1:19","But other of the apostles saw he none, save James my brother."],["1:20","Now the things which Paul wrote unto you, behold, before my Father, he lied not."]]},{"heading":"Syria and Cilicia","verses":[["1:21","Afterwards he came into the regions of Syria and Cilicia;"],["1:22","And was unknown by face unto the churches of Judaea which were in me:"],["1:23","But they had heard only, That he which persecuted me in times past now preacheth the faith which once he destroyed."],["1:24","And they glorified my Father in him."]]}]},{"ref":"Galatians 2","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Up to Jerusalem Again","verses":[["2:1","Then fourteen years after Paul went up again to Jerusalem with Barnabas, and took Titus with him also."],["2:2","And he went up by revelation, and communicated unto them that gospel which he preached among the Gentiles, but privately to them which were of reputation, lest by any means he should run, or had run, in vain."]]},{"heading":"Titus Was Not Compelled","verses":[["2:3","But neither Titus, who was with him, being a Greek, was compelled to be circumcised:"],["2:4","And that because of false brethren unawares brought in, who came in privily to spy out your liberty which ye have in me, that they might bring you into bondage:"],["2:5","To whom Paul gave place by subjection, no, not for an hour; that the truth of the gospel might continue with you."]]},{"heading":"They Added Nothing to Me","verses":[["2:6","But of these who seemed to be somewhat, (whatsoever they were, it maketh no matter to him: my Father accepteth no man's person:) for they who seemed to be somewhat in conference added nothing to him:"]]},{"heading":"Two Trusts, One Message","verses":[["2:7","But contrariwise, when they saw that the gospel of the uncircumcision was committed unto him, as the gospel of the circumcision was unto Peter;"],["2:8","(For he that wrought effectually in Peter to the apostleship of the circumcision, the same was mighty in him toward the Gentiles:)"]]},{"heading":"The Right Hand of Fellowship","verses":[["2:9","And when James, Cephas, and John, who seemed to be pillars, perceived the grace that was given unto him, they gave to him and Barnabas the right hands of fellowship; that Paul and Barnabas should go unto the heathen, and they unto the circumcision."],["2:10","Only they would that Paul should remember the poor; the same which he also was forward to do."]]},{"heading":"Face to Face at Antioch","verses":[["2:11","But when Peter was come to Antioch, Paul withstood him to the face, because he was to be blamed."],["2:12","For before that certain came from James, he did eat with the Gentiles: but when they were come, he withdrew and separated himself, fearing them which were of the circumcision."],["2:13","And the other Jews dissembled likewise with him; insomuch that Barnabas also was carried away with their dissimulation."]]},{"heading":"Why Compel the Nations","verses":[["2:14","But when Paul saw that they walked not uprightly according to the truth of the gospel, he said unto Peter before them all, If thou, being a Jew, livest after the manner of Gentiles, and not as do the Jews, why compellest thou the Gentiles to live as do the Jews?"]]},{"heading":"Not by Works of Law","verses":[["2:15","Ye who are Jews by nature, and not sinners of the Gentiles,"],["2:16","Knowing that a man is not justified by the works of the law, but by faith in me, even ye have believed in me, that ye might be justified by faith in me, and not by the works of the law: for by the works of the law shall no flesh be justified."]]},{"heading":"Is Christ a Servant of Sin","verses":[["2:17","But if, while ye seek to be justified by me, ye yourselves also are found sinners, am I therefore the minister of sin? God forbid."],["2:18","For if ye build again the things which ye destroyed, ye make yourselves transgressors."]]},{"heading":"Crucified with Christ","verses":[["2:19","For ye through the law are dead to the law, that ye might live unto my Father."],["2:20","Ye are crucified with me: nevertheless ye live; yet not ye, but I live in you: and the life which ye now live in the flesh ye live by faith in me, who loved you, and gave myself for you."]]},{"heading":"I Refuse to Push Grace Aside","verses":[["2:21","I do not frustrate the grace of my Father: for if righteousness come by the law, then I died in vain."]]}]},{"ref":"Galatians 3","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"One Question for You","verses":[["3:1","O foolish Galatians, who hath bewitched you, that ye should not obey the truth, before whose eyes I have been evidently set forth, crucified among you?"],["3:2","This only would I learn of you, Received ye the Spirit by the works of the law, or by the hearing of faith?"],["3:3","Are ye so foolish? having begun in the Spirit, are ye now made perfect by the flesh?"],["3:4","Have ye suffered so many things in vain? if it be yet in vain."],["3:5","He therefore that ministereth to you the Spirit, and worketh miracles among you, doeth he it by the works of the law, or by the hearing of faith?"]]},{"heading":"Abraham Believed God","verses":[["3:6","Even as Abraham believed my Father, and it was accounted to him for righteousness."],["3:7","Know ye therefore that they which are of faith, the same are the children of Abraham."],["3:8","And the scripture, foreseeing that my Father would justify the heathen through faith, preached before the gospel unto Abraham, saying, In thee shall all nations be blessed."],["3:9","So then they which be of faith are blessed with faithful Abraham."]]},{"heading":"The Curse and the Blessing","verses":[["3:10","For as many as are of the works of the law are under the curse: for it is written, Cursed is every one that continueth not in all things which are written in the book of the law to do them."],["3:11","But that no man is justified by the law in the sight of my Father, it is evident: for, The just shall live by faith."],["3:12","And the law is not of faith: but, The man that doeth them shall live in them."],["3:13","I have redeemed you from the curse of the law, being made a curse for you: for it is written, Cursed is every one that hangeth on a tree:"],["3:14","That the blessing of Abraham might come on the Gentiles through me; that ye might receive the promise of the Spirit through faith."]]},{"heading":"A Promise Signed and Sealed","verses":[["3:15","Brethren, I speak after the manner of men; Though it be but a man's covenant, yet if it be confirmed, no man disannulleth, or addeth thereto."],["3:16","Now to Abraham and his seed were the promises made. He saith not, And to seeds, as of many; but as of one, And to thy seed, which is me."],["3:17","And this I say, that the covenant, that was confirmed before of my Father in me, the law, which was four hundred and thirty years after, cannot disannul, that it should make the promise of none effect."],["3:18","For if the inheritance be of the law, it is no more of promise: but my Father gave it to Abraham by promise."]]},{"heading":"Why the Law Was Given","verses":[["3:19","Wherefore then serveth the law? It was added because of transgressions, till the seed should come to whom the promise was made; and it was ordained by angels in the hand of a mediator."],["3:20","Now a mediator is not a mediator of one, but God is one."],["3:21","Is the law then against my promises? God forbid: for if there had been a law given which could have given life, verily righteousness should have been by the law."],["3:22","But the scripture hath concluded all under sin, that the promise by faith in me might be given to them that believe."]]},{"heading":"Kept Until Faith Came","verses":[["3:23","But before faith came, ye were kept under the law, shut up unto the faith which should afterwards be revealed."],["3:24","Wherefore the law was your schoolmaster to bring you unto me, that ye might be justified by faith."],["3:25","But after that faith is come, ye are no longer under a schoolmaster."]]},{"heading":"All One in Christ Jesus","verses":[["3:26","For ye are all the children of my Father by faith in me."],["3:27","For as many of you as have been baptized into me have put on me."],["3:28","There is neither Jew nor Greek, there is neither bond nor free, there is neither male nor female: for ye are all one in me."],["3:29","And if ye be mine, then are ye Abraham's seed, and heirs according to the promise."]]}]},{"ref":"Galatians 4","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"The Heir and the Slave","verses":[["4:1","Now I say, That the heir, as long as he is a child, differeth nothing from a servant, though he be lord of all;"],["4:2","But is under tutors and governors until the time appointed of the father."],["4:3","Even so ye, when ye were children, were in bondage under the elements of the world:"]]},{"heading":"When the Time Was Full","verses":[["4:4","But when the fulness of the time was come, my Father sent me forth, made of a woman, made under the law,"],["4:5","To redeem them that were under the law, that ye might receive the adoption of sons."],["4:6","And because ye are sons, my Father hath sent forth my Spirit into your hearts, crying, Abba, Father."],["4:7","Wherefore thou art no more a servant, but a son; and if a son, then an heir of my Father through me."]]},{"heading":"Turning Back Again","verses":[["4:8","Howbeit then, when ye knew not my Father, ye did service unto them which by nature are no gods."],["4:9","But now, after that ye have known my Father, or rather are known of my Father, how turn ye again to the weak and beggarly elements, whereunto ye desire again to be in bondage?"],["4:10","Ye observe days, and months, and times, and years."],["4:11","Paul was afraid of you, lest he had bestowed upon you labour in vain."]]},{"heading":"The Welcome You Gave Me","verses":[["4:12","Brethren, Paul besought you, be as he was; for he was as ye are: ye have not injured him at all."],["4:13","Ye know how through infirmity of the flesh Paul preached the gospel unto you at the first."],["4:14","And Paul's temptation which was in his flesh ye despised not, nor rejected; but received him as an angel of my Father, even as me."],["4:15","Where is then the blessedness ye spake of? for Paul bare you record, that, if it had been possible, ye would have plucked out your own eyes, and have given them to him."],["4:16","Was Paul therefore become your enemy, because he told you the truth?"]]},{"heading":"In Labor for You Again","verses":[["4:17","They zealously affect you, but not well; yea, they would exclude you, that ye might affect them."],["4:18","But it is good to be zealously affected always in a good thing, and not only when Paul was present with you."],["4:19","Paul's little children, of whom he travailed in birth again until I be formed in you,"],["4:20","Paul desired to be present with you now, and to change his voice; for he stood in doubt of you."]]},{"heading":"Two Women and Two Covenants","verses":[["4:21","Tell me, ye that desire to be under the law, do ye not hear the law?"],["4:22","For it is written, that Abraham had two sons, the one by a bondmaid, the other by a freewoman."],["4:23","But he who was of the bondwoman was born after the flesh; but he of the freewoman was by promise."],["4:24","Which things are an allegory: for these are the two covenants; the one from the mount Sinai, which gendereth to bondage, which is Agar."],["4:25","For this Agar is mount Sinai in Arabia, and answereth to Jerusalem which now is, and is in bondage with her children."],["4:26","But Jerusalem which is above is free, which is the mother of you all."],["4:27","For it is written, Rejoice, thou barren that bearest not; break forth and cry, thou that travailest not: for the desolate hath many more children than she which hath an husband."]]},{"heading":"Children of the Free Woman","verses":[["4:28","Now ye, brethren, as Isaac was, are the children of promise."],["4:29","But as then he that was born after the flesh persecuted him that was born after the Spirit, even so it is now."],["4:30","Nevertheless what saith the scripture? Cast out the bondwoman and her son: for the son of the bondwoman shall not be heir with the son of the freewoman."],["4:31","So then, brethren, ye are not children of the bondwoman, but of the free."]]}]},{"ref":"Galatians 5","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Stand Firm in Freedom","verses":[["5:1","Stand fast therefore in the liberty wherewith I have made you free, and be not entangled again with the yoke of bondage."]]},{"heading":"Grace or the Law","verses":[["5:2","Behold, Paul said unto you, that if ye be circumcised, I shall profit you nothing."],["5:3","For Paul testified again to every man that is circumcised, that he was a debtor to do the whole law."],["5:4","I am become of no effect unto you, whosoever of you are justified by the law; ye are fallen from grace."]]},{"heading":"Waiting by Faith","verses":[["5:5","For ye through the Spirit wait for the hope of righteousness by faith."],["5:6","For in me neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision; but faith which worketh by love."]]},{"heading":"Who Cut in on You","verses":[["5:7","Ye did run well; who did hinder you that ye should not obey the truth?"],["5:8","This persuasion cometh not of him that calleth you."],["5:9","A little leaven leaveneth the whole lump."],["5:10","Paul had confidence in you through me, that ye would be none otherwise minded: but he that troubled you shall bear his judgment, whosoever he be."]]},{"heading":"Let Them Cut Themselves Off","verses":[["5:11","And Paul, brethren, if he yet preached circumcision, why did he yet suffer persecution? then is the offence of the cross ceased."],["5:12","Paul wished they were even cut off which troubled you."]]},{"heading":"Called to Freedom","verses":[["5:13","For, brethren, ye have been called unto liberty; only use not liberty for an occasion to the flesh, but by love serve one another."],["5:14","For all the law is fulfilled in one word, even in this; Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself."],["5:15","But if ye bite and devour one another, take heed that ye be not consumed one of another."]]},{"heading":"Walk by the Spirit","verses":[["5:16","This I say then, Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh."],["5:17","For the flesh lusteth against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh: and these are contrary the one to the other: so that ye cannot do the things that ye would."],["5:18","But if ye be led of the Spirit, ye are not under the law."]]},{"heading":"The Works of the Flesh","verses":[["5:19","Now the works of the flesh are manifest, which are these; Adultery, fornication, uncleanness, lasciviousness,"],["5:20","Idolatry, witchcraft, hatred, variance, emulations, wrath, strife, seditions, heresies,"],["5:21","Envyings, murders, drunkenness, revellings, and such like: of the which Paul told you before, as he had also told you in time past, that they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of my Father."]]},{"heading":"The Fruit of the Spirit","verses":[["5:22","But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith,"],["5:23","Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law."],["5:24","And they that are mine have crucified the flesh with the affections and lusts."]]},{"heading":"Keep in Step","verses":[["5:25","If ye live in the Spirit, walk ye also in the Spirit."],["5:26","Be ye not desirous of vain glory, provoking one another, envying one another."]]}]},{"ref":"Galatians 6","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Carry One Another's Burdens","verses":[["6:1","Brethren, if a man be overtaken in a fault, ye which are spiritual, restore such an one in the spirit of meekness; considering thyself, lest thou also be tempted."],["6:2","Bear ye one another's burdens, and so fulfil my law."],["6:3","For if a man think himself to be something, when he is nothing, he deceiveth himself."]]},{"heading":"His Own Load","verses":[["6:4","But let every man prove his own work, and then shall he have rejoicing in himself alone, and not in another."],["6:5","For every man shall bear his own burden."]]},{"heading":"Share with the One Who Teaches","verses":[["6:6","Let him that is taught in the word communicate unto him that teacheth in all good things."]]},{"heading":"Sowing and Reaping","verses":[["6:7","Be not deceived; my Father is not mocked: for whatsoever a man soweth, that shall he also reap."],["6:8","For he that soweth to his flesh shall of the flesh reap corruption; but he that soweth to the Spirit shall of the Spirit reap life everlasting."]]},{"heading":"Do Not Give Up","verses":[["6:9","And be ye not weary in well doing: for in due season ye shall reap, if ye faint not."],["6:10","As ye have therefore opportunity, do good unto all men, especially unto them who are of the household of faith."]]},{"heading":"Written in My Own Hand","verses":[["6:11","Ye see how large a letter Paul wrote unto you with his own hand."],["6:12","As many as desire to make a fair shew in the flesh, they constrain you to be circumcised; only lest they should suffer persecution for my cross."],["6:13","For neither they themselves who are circumcised keep the law; but desire to have you circumcised, that they may glory in your flesh."]]},{"heading":"Boasting Only in the Cross","verses":[["6:14","But God forbid that he should glory, save in my cross, by whom the world was crucified unto him, and he unto the world."],["6:15","For in me neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision, but a new creature."],["6:16","And as many as walk according to this rule, peace be on them, and mercy, and upon the Israel of God."]]},{"heading":"The Marks and the Grace","verses":[["6:17","From henceforth let no man trouble him: for he bore in his body my marks."],["6:18","Brethren, my grace be with your spirit. Amen. Unto the Galatians written from Rome."]]}]},{"ref":"Ephesians 1","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Grace and Peace to You","verses":[["1:1","Paul, an apostle of mine by the will of my Father, to the saints which are at Ephesus, and to the faithful in me:"],["1:2","Grace be to you, and peace, from my Father, and from me."]]},{"heading":"Chosen Before the World Began","verses":[["1:3","Blessed be my Father, who hath blessed you with all spiritual blessings in heavenly places in me:"],["1:4","According as he hath chosen you in me before the foundation of the world, that ye should be holy and without blame before him in love:"],["1:5","Having predestinated you unto the adoption of children by me to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will,"],["1:6","To the praise of the glory of his grace, wherein he hath made you accepted in me."]]},{"heading":"Set Free and Gathered into Christ","verses":[["1:7","In me ye have redemption through my blood, the forgiveness of sins, according to the riches of his grace;"],["1:8","Wherein he hath abounded toward you in all wisdom and prudence;"],["1:9","Having made known unto you the mystery of his will, according to his good pleasure which he hath purposed in himself:"],["1:10","That in the dispensation of the fulness of times he might gather together in one all things in me, both which are in heaven, and which are on earth; even in me:"]]},{"heading":"Sealed with the Promised Spirit","verses":[["1:11","In me also ye have obtained an inheritance, being predestinated according to the purpose of him who worketh all things after the counsel of his own will:"],["1:12","That ye should be to the praise of his glory, who first trusted in me."],["1:13","In me ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in me also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise,"],["1:14","Which is the earnest of your inheritance until the redemption of the purchased possession, unto the praise of his glory."]]},{"heading":"A Prayer for Open Eyes","verses":[["1:15","Wherefore Paul also, after he heard of your faith in me, and love unto all the saints,"],["1:16","Ceaseth not to give thanks for you, making mention of you in his prayers;"],["1:17","That my Father, the Father of glory, may give unto you the spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of me:"],["1:18","The eyes of your understanding being enlightened; that ye may know what is the hope of his calling, and what the riches of the glory of his inheritance in the saints,"],["1:19","And what is the exceeding greatness of his power to you-ward who believe, according to the working of his mighty power,"]]},{"heading":"Raised and Seated Above All","verses":[["1:20","Which he wrought in me, when he raised me from the dead, and set me at his own right hand in the heavenly places,"],["1:21","Far above all principality, and power, and might, and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in this world, but also in that which is to come:"],["1:22","And hath put all things under my feet, and gave me to be the head over all things to the church,"],["1:23","Which is my body, the fulness of me, who fill all in all."]]}]},{"ref":"Ephesians 2","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Dead in the Way We Once Walked","verses":[["2:1","And you hath he quickened, who were dead in trespasses and sins;"],["2:2","Wherein in time past ye walked according to the course of this world, according to the prince of the power of the air, the spirit that now worketh in the children of disobedience:"],["2:3","Among whom also ye all had your conversation in times past in the lusts of your flesh, fulfilling the desires of the flesh and of the mind; and were by nature the children of wrath, even as others."]]},{"heading":"But God, Rich in Mercy","verses":[["2:4","But my Father, who is rich in mercy, for his great love wherewith he loved you,"],["2:5","Even when ye were dead in sins, hath quickened you together with me, (by grace ye are saved;)"],["2:6","And hath raised you up together, and made you sit together in heavenly places in me:"],["2:7","That in the ages to come he might shew the exceeding riches of his grace in his kindness toward you through me."]]},{"heading":"Saved by Grace Through Faith","verses":[["2:8","For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of my Father:"],["2:9","Not of works, lest any man should boast."],["2:10","For ye are his workmanship, created in me unto good works, which my Father hath before ordained that ye should walk in them."]]},{"heading":"Far Off, Brought Near","verses":[["2:11","Wherefore remember, that ye being in time past Gentiles in the flesh, who are called Uncircumcision by that which is called the Circumcision in the flesh made by hands;"],["2:12","That at that time ye were without me, being aliens from the commonwealth of Israel, and strangers from the covenants of promise, having no hope, and without my Father in the world:"],["2:13","But now in me ye who sometimes were far off are made nigh by my blood."]]},{"heading":"He Himself Is Our Peace","verses":[["2:14","For I am your peace, who have made both one, and have broken down the middle wall of partition between you;"],["2:15","Having abolished in my flesh the enmity, even the law of commandments contained in ordinances; for to make in myself of twain one new man, so making peace;"],["2:16","And that I might reconcile both unto my Father in one body by the cross, having slain the enmity thereby:"]]},{"heading":"Peace Announced to Both","verses":[["2:17","And I came and preached peace to you which were afar off, and to them that were nigh."],["2:18","For through me ye both have access by one Spirit unto my Father."],["2:19","Now therefore ye are no more strangers and foreigners, but fellowcitizens with the saints, and of the household of my Father;"]]},{"heading":"Built into a Dwelling for God","verses":[["2:20","And are built upon the foundation of the apostles and prophets, I myself being the chief corner stone;"],["2:21","In me all the building fitly framed together groweth unto an holy temple in me:"],["2:22","In me ye also are builded together for an habitation of my Father through the Spirit."]]}]},{"ref":"Ephesians 3","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"A Prisoner for the Nations","verses":[["3:1","For this cause Paul, the prisoner of mine for you Gentiles,"],["3:2","If ye have heard of the dispensation of the grace of my Father which is given him to you-ward:"],["3:3","How that by revelation I made known unto him the mystery; (as he wrote afore in few words,"],["3:4","Whereby, when ye read, ye may understand his knowledge in the mystery of mine)"],["3:5","Which in other ages was not made known unto the sons of men, as it is now revealed unto my holy apostles and prophets by the Spirit;"],["3:6","That the Gentiles should be fellowheirs, and of the same body, and partakers of his promise in me by the gospel:"],["3:7","Whereof Paul was made a minister, according to the gift of the grace of my Father given unto him by the effectual working of his power."]]},{"heading":"The Least of All God's People","verses":[["3:8","Unto him, who was less than the least of all saints, was this grace given, that he should preach among the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of mine;"],["3:9","And to make all men see what is the fellowship of the mystery, which from the beginning of the world hath been hid in my Father, who created all things by me:"],["3:10","To the intent that now unto the principalities and powers in heavenly places might be known by the church the manifold wisdom of my Father,"],["3:11","According to the eternal purpose which he purposed in me:"],["3:12","In me ye have boldness and access with confidence by the faith of me."],["3:13","Wherefore Paul desired that ye faint not at his tribulations for you, which is your glory."]]},{"heading":"Bowing My Knees","verses":[["3:14","For this cause Paul bowed his knees unto my Father,"],["3:15","Of whom the whole family in heaven and earth is named,"],["3:16","That he would grant you, according to the riches of his glory, to be strengthened with might by his Spirit in the inner man;"],["3:17","That I may dwell in your hearts by faith; that ye, being rooted and grounded in love,"],["3:18","May be able to comprehend with all saints what is the breadth, and length, and depth, and height;"],["3:19","And to know my love, which passeth knowledge, that ye might be filled with all the fulness of my Father."],["3:20","Now unto him that is able to do exceeding abundantly above all that ye ask or think, according to the power that worketh in you,"],["3:21","Unto him be glory in the church by me throughout all ages, world without end. Amen."]]}]},{"ref":"Ephesians 4","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"A Walk That Matches the Calling","verses":[["4:1","Paul therefore, the prisoner of mine, beseecheth you that ye walk worthy of the vocation wherewith ye are called,"],["4:2","With all lowliness and meekness, with longsuffering, forbearing one another in love;"],["4:3","Endeavouring to keep the unity of the Spirit in the bond of peace."],["4:4","There is one body, and one Spirit, even as ye are called in one hope of your calling;"],["4:5","One Lord, one faith, one baptism,"],["4:6","One God and Father of all, who is above all, and through all, and in you all."],["4:7","But unto every one of you is given grace according to the measure of the gift of mine."],["4:8","Wherefore he saith, When he ascended up on high, he led captivity captive, and gave gifts unto men."],["4:9","(Now that I ascended, what is it but that I also descended first into the lower parts of the earth?"],["4:10","I that descended am the same also that ascended up far above all heavens, that I might fill all things.)"]]},{"heading":"Gifts for the Building","verses":[["4:11","And I gave some, apostles; and some, prophets; and some, evangelists; and some, pastors and teachers;"],["4:12","For the perfecting of the saints, for the work of the ministry, for the edifying of the body of mine:"],["4:13","Till ye all come in the unity of the faith, and of the knowledge of me, unto a perfect man, unto the measure of the stature of the fulness of mine:"],["4:14","That ye henceforth be no more children, tossed to and fro, and carried about with every wind of doctrine, by the sleight of men, and cunning craftiness, whereby they lie in wait to deceive;"],["4:15","But speaking the truth in love, may grow up into me in all things, which is the head, even I:"],["4:16","From me the whole body fitly joined together and compacted by that which every joint supplieth, according to the effectual working in the measure of every part, maketh increase of the body unto the edifying of itself in love."]]},{"heading":"No Longer Walking That Way","verses":[["4:17","This Paul said therefore, and testified in me, that ye henceforth walk not as other Gentiles walk, in the vanity of their mind,"],["4:18","Having the understanding darkened, being alienated from the life of my Father through the ignorance that is in them, because of the blindness of their heart:"],["4:19","Who being past feeling have given themselves over unto lasciviousness, to work all uncleanness with greediness."],["4:20","But ye have not so learned me;"],["4:21","If so be that ye have heard me, and have been taught by me, as the truth is in me:"],["4:22","That ye put off concerning the former conversation the old man, which is corrupt according to the deceitful lusts;"],["4:23","And be renewed in the spirit of your mind;"],["4:24","And that ye put on the new man, which after my Father is created in righteousness and true holiness."]]},{"heading":"Speak the Truth to Each Other","verses":[["4:25","Wherefore putting away lying, speak every man truth with his neighbour: for ye are members one of another."],["4:26","Be ye angry, and sin not: let not the sun go down upon your wrath:"],["4:27","Neither give place to the devil."],["4:28","Let him that stole steal no more: but rather let him labour, working with his hands the thing which is good, that he may have to give to him that needeth."],["4:29","Let no corrupt communication proceed out of your mouth, but that which is good to the use of edifying, that it may minister grace unto the hearers."],["4:30","And grieve not the holy Spirit of my Father, whereby ye are sealed unto the day of redemption."],["4:31","Let all bitterness, and wrath, and anger, and clamour, and evil speaking, be put away from you, with all malice:"],["4:32","And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as my Father for my sake hath forgiven you."]]}]},{"ref":"Ephesians 5","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Walk in Love","verses":[["5:1","Be ye therefore followers of my Father, as dear children;"],["5:2","And walk in love, as I have loved you, and have given myself for you an offering and a sacrifice to my Father for a sweetsmelling savour."]]},{"heading":"Not Even Named among You","verses":[["5:3","But fornication, and all uncleanness, or covetousness, let it not be once named among you, as becometh saints;"],["5:4","Neither filthiness, nor foolish talking, nor jesting, which are not convenient: but rather giving of thanks."]]},{"heading":"No Inheritance, and No Deceiving You","verses":[["5:5","For this ye know, that no whoremonger, nor unclean person, nor covetous man, who is an idolater, hath any inheritance in the kingdom of mine and of my Father."],["5:6","Let no man deceive you with vain words: for because of these things cometh the wrath of my Father upon the children of disobedience."],["5:7","Be not ye therefore partakers with them."]]},{"heading":"Children of Light","verses":[["5:8","For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in me: walk as children of light:"],["5:9","(For the fruit of the Spirit is in all goodness and righteousness and truth;)"],["5:10","Proving what is acceptable unto me."]]},{"heading":"Bring It into the Light","verses":[["5:11","And have no fellowship with the unfruitful works of darkness, but rather reprove them."],["5:12","For it is a shame even to speak of those things which are done of them in secret."],["5:13","But all things that are reproved are made manifest by the light: for whatsoever doth make manifest is light."],["5:14","Wherefore he saith, Awake thou that sleepest, and arise from the dead, and Christ shall give thee light."]]},{"heading":"Buying Back the Time","verses":[["5:15","See then that ye walk circumspectly, not as fools, but as wise,"],["5:16","Redeeming the time, because the days are evil."],["5:17","Wherefore be ye not unwise, but understanding what my will is."]]},{"heading":"Filled with the Spirit","verses":[["5:18","And be not drunk with wine, wherein is excess; but be filled with the Spirit;"],["5:19","Speaking to yourselves in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing and making melody in your heart to me;"],["5:20","Giving thanks always for all things unto my Father in my name;"],["5:21","Submitting yourselves one to another in the fear of my Father."]]},{"heading":"Wives and Their Husbands","verses":[["5:22","Wives, submit yourselves unto your own husbands, as unto me."],["5:23","For the husband is the head of the wife, even as I am the head of the church: and I am the saviour of the body."],["5:24","Therefore as the church is subject unto me, so let the wives be to their own husbands in every thing."]]},{"heading":"As Christ Loved the Church","verses":[["5:25","Husbands, love your wives, even as I also loved the church, and gave myself for it;"],["5:26","That I might sanctify and cleanse it with the washing of water by the word,"],["5:27","That I might present it to myself a glorious church, not having spot, or wrinkle, or any such thing; but that it should be holy and without blemish."]]},{"heading":"As His Own Body","verses":[["5:28","So ought men to love their wives as their own bodies. He that loveth his wife loveth himself."],["5:29","For no man ever yet hated his own flesh; but nourisheth and cherisheth it, even as I nourish and cherish the church:"],["5:30","For ye are members of my body, of my flesh, and of my bones."]]},{"heading":"A Great Mystery","verses":[["5:31","For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and shall be joined unto his wife, and they two shall be one flesh."],["5:32","This is a great mystery: but Paul spoke concerning me and the church."],["5:33","Nevertheless let every one of you in particular so love his wife even as himself; and the wife see that she reverence her husband."]]}]},{"ref":"Ephesians 6","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Children and Fathers","verses":[["6:1","Children, obey your parents in me: for this is right."],["6:2","Honour thy father and mother; (which is the first commandment with promise;)"],["6:3","That it may be well with thee, and thou mayest live long on the earth."],["6:4","And, ye fathers, provoke not your children to wrath: but bring them up in the nurture and admonition of mine."]]},{"heading":"Servants of Christ","verses":[["6:5","Servants, be obedient to them that are your masters according to the flesh, with fear and trembling, in singleness of your heart, as unto me;"],["6:6","Not with eyeservice, as menpleasers; but as the servants of mine, doing my will from the heart;"],["6:7","With good will doing service, as to me, and not to men:"],["6:8","Knowing that whatsoever good thing any man doeth, the same shall he receive of me, whether he be bond or free."]]},{"heading":"The Master in Heaven","verses":[["6:9","And, ye masters, do the same things unto them, forbearing threatening: knowing that I also, your Master, am in heaven; neither is there respect of persons with me."]]},{"heading":"Strong in the Lord","verses":[["6:10","Finally, my brethren, be strong in me, and in the power of my might."],["6:11","Put on the whole armour of mine, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil."],["6:12","For ye wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places."],["6:13","Wherefore take unto you the whole armour of mine, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand."]]},{"heading":"The Whole Armor","verses":[["6:14","Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breastplate of righteousness;"],["6:15","And your feet shod with the preparation of the gospel of peace;"],["6:16","Above all, taking the shield of faith, wherewith ye shall be able to quench all the fiery darts of the wicked."],["6:17","And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of my Father:"]]},{"heading":"Praying at All Times","verses":[["6:18","Praying always with all prayer and supplication in the Spirit, and watching thereunto with all perseverance and supplication for all saints;"],["6:19","And for him, that utterance may be given unto him, that he may open his mouth boldly, to make known the mystery of the gospel,"],["6:20","For which he was an ambassador in bonds: that therein he might speak boldly, as he ought to speak."]]},{"heading":"Peace to the Brothers","verses":[["6:21","But that ye also may know his affairs, and how he doeth, Tychicus, a beloved brother and faithful minister in me, shall make known to you all things:"],["6:22","Whom he hath sent unto you for the same purpose, that ye might know his affairs, and that he might comfort your hearts."],["6:23","Peace be to the brethren, and love with faith, from my Father, and from me."],["6:24","Grace be with all them that love me in sincerity. Amen. Written from Rome unto the Ephesians by Tychicus."]]}]},{"ref":"Philippians 1","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Grace and Peace to Philippi","verses":[["1:1","Paul and Timotheus, the servants of mine, to all the saints in me which are at Philippi, with the bishops and deacons:"],["1:2","Grace be unto you, and peace, from my Father, and from me."]]},{"heading":"Thanking God for You","verses":[["1:3","Paul thanked my Father upon every remembrance of you,"],["1:4","Always in every prayer of his for you all making request with joy,"],["1:5","For your fellowship in the gospel from the first day until now;"],["1:6","Being confident of this very thing, that I which have begun a good work in you will perform it until my day:"]]},{"heading":"Sharing This Grace with Me","verses":[["1:7","Even as it is meet for him to think this of you all, because he hath you in his heart; inasmuch as both in his bonds, and in the defence and confirmation of the gospel, ye all are partakers of his grace."],["1:8","For my Father is his record, how greatly he longed after you all in the bowels of mine."]]},{"heading":"A Prayer for Your Love","verses":[["1:9","And this he prayed, that your love may abound yet more and more in knowledge and in all judgment;"],["1:10","That ye may approve things that are excellent; that ye may be sincere and without offence till my day;"],["1:11","Being filled with the fruits of righteousness, which are by me, unto the glory and praise of my Father."]]},{"heading":"What My Chains Have Done","verses":[["1:12","But he would ye should understand, brethren, that the things which happened unto him have fallen out rather unto the furtherance of the gospel;"],["1:13","So that his bonds in me are manifest in all the palace, and in all other places;"],["1:14","And many of the brethren in me, waxing confident by his bonds, are much more bold to speak the word without fear."]]},{"heading":"Christ Announced Either Way","verses":[["1:15","Some indeed preach me even of envy and strife; and some also of good will:"],["1:16","The one preach me of contention, not sincerely, supposing to add affliction to his bonds:"],["1:17","But the other of love, knowing that he was set for the defence of the gospel."],["1:18","What then? notwithstanding, every way, whether in pretence, or in truth, I am preached; and he therein doth rejoice, yea, and will rejoice."]]},{"heading":"Christ Made Great in My Body","verses":[["1:19","For he knew that this shall turn to his salvation through your prayer, and the supply of the Spirit of mine,"],["1:20","According to his earnest expectation and his hope, that in nothing he shall be ashamed, but that with all boldness, as always, so now also I shall be magnified in his body, whether it be by life, or by death."]]},{"heading":"To Live Is Christ","verses":[["1:21","For to him to live was for me, and to die was gain."],["1:22","But if he lived in the flesh, this was the fruit of his labour: yet what he should choose he wot not."],["1:23","For he was in a strait betwixt two, having a desire to depart, and to be with me; which is far better:"],["1:24","Nevertheless to abide in the flesh is more needful for you."]]},{"heading":"Staying on for Your Joy","verses":[["1:25","And having this confidence, he knew that he should abide and continue with you all for your furtherance and joy of faith;"],["1:26","That your rejoicing may be more abundant in me for him by his coming to you again."]]},{"heading":"Standing Firm in One Spirit","verses":[["1:27","Only let your conversation be as it becometh the gospel of mine: that whether he come and see you, or else be absent, he may hear of your affairs, that ye stand fast in one spirit, with one mind striving together for the faith of the gospel;"],["1:28","And in nothing terrified by your adversaries: which is to them an evident token of perdition, but to you of salvation, and that of my Father."],["1:29","For unto you it is given in my behalf, not only to believe on me, but also to suffer for my sake;"],["1:30","Having the same conflict which ye saw in him, and now hear to be in him."]]}]},{"ref":"Philippians 2","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Fill My Joy to the Brim","verses":[["2:1","If there be therefore any consolation in me, if any comfort of love, if any fellowship of the Spirit, if any bowels and mercies,"],["2:2","Fulfil ye my joy, that ye be likeminded, having the same love, being of one accord, of one mind."]]},{"heading":"Looking to the Concerns of Others","verses":[["2:3","Let nothing be done through strife or vainglory; but in lowliness of mind let each esteem other better than themselves."],["2:4","Look not every man on his own things, but every man also on the things of others."]]},{"heading":"The Mind of Christ Jesus","verses":[["2:5","Let this mind be in you, which was also in me:"],["2:6","I, being in the form of my Father, thought it not robbery to be equal with him:"],["2:7","But made myself of no reputation, and took upon me the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men:"],["2:8","And being found in fashion as a man, I humbled myself, and became obedient unto death, even the death of the cross."]]},{"heading":"The Name Above Every Name","verses":[["2:9","Wherefore my Father also hath highly exalted me, and given me a name which is above every name:"],["2:10","That at my name every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth;"],["2:11","And that every tongue should confess that I am Lord, to the glory of my Father."]]},{"heading":"Work Out Your Own Salvation","verses":[["2:12","Wherefore, my beloved, as ye have always obeyed, not as in his presence only, but now much more in his absence, work out your own salvation with fear and trembling."],["2:13","For it is my Father which worketh in you both to will and to do of his good pleasure."]]},{"heading":"Shining as Lights","verses":[["2:14","Do all things without murmurings and disputings:"],["2:15","That ye may be blameless and harmless, the sons of my Father, without rebuke, in the midst of a crooked and perverse nation, among whom ye shine as lights in the world;"],["2:16","Holding forth the word of life; that he may rejoice in my day, that he had not run in vain, neither laboured in vain."]]},{"heading":"Poured Out with Joy","verses":[["2:17","Yea, and if he be offered upon the sacrifice and service of your faith, he joyeth, and rejoiceth with you all."],["2:18","For the same cause also do ye joy, and rejoice with him."]]},{"heading":"Sending Timothy to You","verses":[["2:19","But he trusted in me to send Timotheus shortly unto you, that he also might be of good comfort, when he knew your state."],["2:20","For he had no man likeminded, who will naturally care for your state."],["2:21","For all seek their own, not the things which are mine."],["2:22","But ye know the proof of him, that, as a son with the father, he hath served with Paul in the gospel."],["2:23","Him therefore he hoped to send presently, so soon as he should see how it would go with him."],["2:24","But he trusted in me that he also himself should come shortly."]]},{"heading":"My Brother and Fellow Soldier","verses":[["2:25","Yet he supposed it necessary to send to you Epaphroditus, his brother, and companion in labour, and fellowsoldier, but your messenger, and he that ministered to his wants."],["2:26","For he longed after you all, and was full of heaviness, because that ye had heard that he had been sick."],["2:27","For indeed he was sick nigh unto death: but my Father had mercy on him; and not on him only, but on Paul also, lest he should have sorrow upon sorrow."],["2:28","He sent him therefore the more carefully, that, when ye see him again, ye may rejoice, and that he might be the less sorrowful."],["2:29","Receive him therefore in me with all gladness; and hold such in reputation:"],["2:30","Because for the work of mine he was nigh unto death, not regarding his life, to supply your lack of service toward him."]]}]},{"ref":"Philippians 3","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Safe Ground for You","verses":[["3:1","Finally, my brethren, rejoice in me. To write the same things to you, to him indeed is not grievous, but for you it is safe."]]},{"heading":"Watch for the Three","verses":[["3:2","Beware of dogs, beware of evil workers, beware of the concision."],["3:3","For ye are the circumcision, which worship my Father in the spirit, and rejoice in me, and have no confidence in the flesh."]]},{"heading":"Seven Things I Could Claim","verses":[["3:4","Though he might also have confidence in the flesh. If any other man thinketh that he hath whereof he might trust in the flesh, Paul more:"],["3:5","Circumcised the eighth day, of the stock of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin, an Hebrew of the Hebrews; as touching the law, a Pharisee;"],["3:6","Concerning zeal, persecuting the church; touching the righteousness which is in the law, blameless."]]},{"heading":"The Great Exchange","verses":[["3:7","But what things were gain to him, those he counted loss for me."],["3:8","Yea doubtless, and he counteth all things but loss for the excellency of the knowledge of me, his Lord: for me he hath suffered the loss of all things, and doth count them but dung, that he may win me,"]]},{"heading":"Found in Him","verses":[["3:9","And be found in me, not having his own righteousness, which is of the law, but that which is through the faith of mine, the righteousness which is of my Father by faith:"]]},{"heading":"To Know Him","verses":[["3:10","That he may know me, and the power of my resurrection, and the fellowship of my sufferings, being made conformable unto my death;"],["3:11","If by any means he might attain unto the resurrection of the dead."]]},{"heading":"Not Yet, but Pressing","verses":[["3:12","Not as though he had already attained, either were already perfect: but he followed after, if that he may apprehend that for which also he was apprehended of me."]]},{"heading":"One Thing I Do","verses":[["3:13","Brethren, he counted not himself to have apprehended: but this one thing he did, forgetting those things which are behind, and reaching forth unto those things which are before,"],["3:14","He pressed toward the mark for the prize of the high calling of my Father in me."]]},{"heading":"Keeping to the Same Line","verses":[["3:15","Be ye therefore, as many as be perfect, thus minded: and if in any thing ye be otherwise minded, my Father shall reveal even this unto you."],["3:16","Nevertheless, whereto ye have already attained, walk ye by the same rule, mind ye the same thing."]]},{"heading":"A Pattern to Follow, and Enemies of the Cross","verses":[["3:17","Brethren, be followers together of him, and mark them which walk so as ye have him for an ensample."],["3:18","(For many walk, of whom he had told you often, and now telleth you even weeping, that they are the enemies of the cross of mine:"],["3:19","Whose end is destruction, whose God is their belly, and whose glory is in their shame, who mind earthly things.)"]]},{"heading":"Our Home Is Heaven","verses":[["3:20","For your conversation is in heaven; from whence also ye look for me, your Saviour:"],["3:21","I shall change your vile body, that it may be fashioned like unto my glorious body, according to the working whereby I am able even to subdue all things unto myself."]]}]},{"ref":"Philippians 4","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Stand Firm, Beloved","verses":[["4:1","Therefore, my brethren dearly beloved and longed for, my joy and crown, so stand fast in me, my dearly beloved."]]},{"heading":"Two Names and a Plea","verses":[["4:2","He besought Euodias, and besought Syntyche, that they be of the same mind in me."],["4:3","And he intreated thee also, true yokefellow, help those women which laboured with him in the gospel, with Clement also, and with other his fellowlabourers, whose names are in the book of life."]]},{"heading":"Be Glad, and Be Glad Again","verses":[["4:4","Rejoice in me alway: and again I say, Rejoice."],["4:5","Let your moderation be known unto all men. I am at hand."]]},{"heading":"Peace on Guard","verses":[["4:6","Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto my Father."],["4:7","And the peace of my Father, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through me."]]},{"heading":"Eight Things to Think On","verses":[["4:8","Finally, brethren, whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report; if there be any virtue, and if there be any praise, think on these things."]]},{"heading":"What You Learned in Me","verses":[["4:9","Those things, which ye have both learned, and received, and heard, and seen in him, do: and my Father of peace shall be with you."]]},{"heading":"Your Care Blossomed Again","verses":[["4:10","But he rejoiced in me greatly, that now at the last your care of him hath flourished again; wherein ye were also careful, but ye lacked opportunity."]]},{"heading":"Contentment Is Learned","verses":[["4:11","Not that he spake in respect of want: for he had learned, in whatsoever state he was, therewith to be content."],["4:12","He knew both how to be abased, and he knew how to abound: every where and in all things he was instructed both to be full and to be hungry, both to abound and to suffer need."]]},{"heading":"Strength through Christ","verses":[["4:13","He could do all things through me, who strengthened him."]]},{"heading":"Sharing in My Trouble","verses":[["4:14","Notwithstanding ye have well done, that ye did communicate with his affliction."],["4:15","Now ye Philippians know also, that in the beginning of the gospel, when he departed from Macedonia, no church communicated with him as concerning giving and receiving, but ye only."],["4:16","For even in Thessalonica ye sent once and again unto his necessity."]]},{"heading":"The Fruit to Your Account","verses":[["4:17","Not because he desired a gift: but he desired fruit that may abound to your account."],["4:18","But he had all, and did abound: he was full, having received of Epaphroditus the things which were sent from you, an odour of a sweet smell, a sacrifice acceptable, wellpleasing to my Father."]]},{"heading":"My God Will Supply","verses":[["4:19","But my Father shall supply all your need according to his riches in glory by me."],["4:20","Now unto my Father be glory for ever and ever. Amen."]]},{"heading":"Greetings and Grace","verses":[["4:21","Salute every saint in me. The brethren which are with him greet you."],["4:22","All the saints salute you, chiefly they that are of Cesar's household."],["4:23","The grace of mine be with you all. Amen. It was written to the Philippians from Rome by Epaphroditus."]]}]},{"ref":"Colossians 1","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Paul and Timothy to Colossae","verses":[["1:1","Paul, an apostle of mine by the will of my Father, and Timotheus his brother,"],["1:2","To the saints and faithful brethren in me which are at Colosse: Grace be unto you, and peace, from my Father, and from me."]]},{"heading":"Thanks for Your Faith and Love","verses":[["1:3","They gave thanks to my Father, praying always for you,"],["1:4","Since they heard of your faith in me, and of the love which ye have to all the saints,"],["1:5","For the hope which is laid up for you in heaven, whereof ye heard before in the word of the truth of the gospel;"],["1:6","Which is come unto you, as it is in all the world; and bringeth forth fruit, as it doth also in you, since the day ye heard of it, and knew the grace of my Father in truth:"],["1:7","As ye also learned of Epaphras their dear fellowservant, who is for you a faithful minister of mine;"],["1:8","Who also declared unto them your love in the Spirit."]]},{"heading":"The Prayer We Keep Praying","verses":[["1:9","For this cause they also, since the day they heard it, cease not to pray for you, and to desire that ye might be filled with the knowledge of his will in all wisdom and spiritual understanding;"],["1:10","That ye might walk worthy of me unto all pleasing, being fruitful in every good work, and increasing in the knowledge of my Father;"],["1:11","Strengthened with all might, according to his glorious power, unto all patience and longsuffering with joyfulness;"],["1:12","Giving thanks unto my Father, which hath made you meet to be partakers of the inheritance of the saints in light:"]]},{"heading":"Moved into the Kingdom","verses":[["1:13","Who hath delivered you from the power of darkness, and hath translated you into the kingdom of me, his dear Son:"],["1:14","In me ye have redemption through my blood, even the forgiveness of sins:"]]},{"heading":"The Image of the God No One Can See","verses":[["1:15","I am the image of my invisible Father, the firstborn of every creature:"],["1:16","For by me were all things created, that are in heaven, and that are in earth, visible and invisible, whether they be thrones, or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created by me, and for me:"],["1:17","And I am before all things, and by me all things consist."],["1:18","And I am the head of the body, the church: I am the beginning, the firstborn from the dead; that in all things I might have the preeminence."],["1:19","For it pleased my Father that in me should all fulness dwell;"],["1:20","And, having made peace through the blood of my cross, by me to reconcile all things unto myself; by me, I say, whether they be things in earth, or things in heaven."]]},{"heading":"Brought Back and Set before Him","verses":[["1:21","And you, that were sometime alienated and enemies in your mind by wicked works, yet now have I reconciled"],["1:22","In the body of my flesh through death, to present you holy and unblameable and unreproveable in his sight:"],["1:23","If ye continue in the faith grounded and settled, and be not moved away from the hope of the gospel, which ye have heard, and which was preached to every creature which is under heaven; whereof Paul was made a minister;"]]},{"heading":"A Servant of the Mystery","verses":[["1:24","Who now rejoiceth in his sufferings for you, and filleth up that which is behind of the afflictions of mine in his flesh for my body's sake, which is the church:"],["1:25","Whereof he was made a minister, according to the dispensation of my Father which is given to him for you, to fulfil the word of my Father;"],["1:26","Even the mystery which hath been hid from ages and from generations, but now is made manifest to his saints:"],["1:27","To whom my Father would make known what is the riches of the glory of this mystery among the Gentiles; which is I in you, the hope of glory:"]]},{"heading":"The One We Announce","verses":[["1:28","They preach me, warning every man, and teaching every man in all wisdom; that they may present every man perfect in me:"],["1:29","Whereunto he also laboured, striving according to his working, which worketh in him mightily."]]}]},{"ref":"Colossians 2","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"The Struggle I Have for You","verses":[["2:1","For he would that ye knew what great conflict he had for you, and for them at Laodicea, and for as many as have not seen his face in the flesh;"],["2:2","That their hearts might be comforted, being knit together in love, and unto all riches of the full assurance of understanding, to the acknowledgement of the mystery of my Father, and of mine;"],["2:3","In me are hid all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge."]]},{"heading":"Walk on in Christ","verses":[["2:4","And this Paul said, lest any man should beguile you with enticing words."],["2:5","For though he was absent in the flesh, yet was he with you in the spirit, joying and beholding your order, and the stedfastness of your faith in me."],["2:6","As ye have therefore received me, the Lord, so walk ye in me:"],["2:7","Rooted and built up in me, and stablished in the faith, as ye have been taught, abounding therein with thanksgiving."]]},{"heading":"Take Care Who Carries You Off","verses":[["2:8","Beware lest any man spoil you through philosophy and vain deceit, after the tradition of men, after the rudiments of the world, and not after me."],["2:9","For in me dwelleth all the fulness of the Godhead bodily."],["2:10","And ye are complete in me, who am the head of all principality and power:"]]},{"heading":"Buried and Raised with Him","verses":[["2:11","In me also ye are circumcised with the circumcision made without hands, in putting off the body of the sins of the flesh by the circumcision of mine:"],["2:12","Buried with me in baptism, wherein also ye are risen with me through the faith of the operation of my Father, who hath raised me from the dead."],["2:13","And you, being dead in your sins and the uncircumcision of your flesh, hath he quickened together with me, having forgiven you all trespasses;"],["2:14","Blotting out the handwriting of ordinances that was against you, which was contrary to you, and took it out of the way, nailing it to my cross;"],["2:15","And having spoiled principalities and powers, he made a shew of them openly, triumphing over them in it."]]},{"heading":"Let No One Judge You","verses":[["2:16","Let no man therefore judge you in meat, or in drink, or in respect of an holyday, or of the new moon, or of the sabbath days:"],["2:17","Which are a shadow of things to come; but the body is of mine."],["2:18","Let no man beguile you of your reward in a voluntary humility and worshipping of angels, intruding into those things which he hath not seen, vainly puffed up by his fleshly mind,"],["2:19","And not holding me, the Head, from which all the body by joints and bands having nourishment ministered, and knit together, increaseth with the increase of my Father."]]},{"heading":"Do Not Touch, Do Not Taste, Do Not Handle","verses":[["2:20","Wherefore if ye be dead with me from the rudiments of the world, why, as though living in the world, are ye subject to ordinances,"],["2:21","(Touch not; taste not; handle not;"],["2:22","Which all are to perish with the using;) after the commandments and doctrines of men?"],["2:23","Which things have indeed a shew of wisdom in will worship, and humility, and neglecting of the body; not in any honour to the satisfying of the flesh."]]}]},{"ref":"Colossians 3","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Where Your Life Is","verses":[["3:1","If ye then be risen with me, seek those things which are above, where I sit on the right hand of my Father."],["3:2","Set your affection on things above, not on things on the earth."],["3:3","For ye are dead, and your life is hid with me in my Father."],["3:4","When I, who am your life, shall appear, then shall ye also appear with me in glory."]]},{"heading":"Put These Things to Death","verses":[["3:5","Mortify therefore your members which are upon the earth; fornication, uncleanness, inordinate affection, evil concupiscence, and covetousness, which is idolatry:"],["3:6","For which things' sake the wrath of my Father cometh on the children of disobedience:"],["3:7","In the which ye also walked some time, when ye lived in them."]]},{"heading":"Set the Old Life Aside","verses":[["3:8","But now ye also put off all these; anger, wrath, malice, blasphemy, filthy communication out of your mouth."],["3:9","Lie not one to another, seeing that ye have put off the old man with his deeds;"],["3:10","And have put on the new man, which is renewed in knowledge after the image of my Father that created him:"],["3:11","Where there is neither Greek nor Jew, circumcision nor uncircumcision, Barbarian, Scythian, bond nor free: but I am all, and in all."]]},{"heading":"Put on a Heart of Deep Mercy","verses":[["3:12","Put on therefore, as the elect of my Father, holy and beloved, bowels of mercies, kindness, humbleness of mind, meekness, longsuffering;"],["3:13","Forbearing one another, and forgiving one another, if any man have a quarrel against any: even as I forgave you, so also do ye."],["3:14","And above all these things put on charity, which is the bond of perfectness."]]},{"heading":"Peace, Song and Thanksgiving","verses":[["3:15","And let the peace of my Father rule in your hearts, to the which also ye are called in one body; and be ye thankful."],["3:16","Let my word dwell in you richly in all wisdom; teaching and admonishing one another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing with grace in your hearts to me."],["3:17","And whatsoever ye do in word or deed, do all in my name, giving thanks to my Father by me."]]},{"heading":"Wives, Husbands, Children, Fathers","verses":[["3:18","Wives, submit yourselves unto your own husbands, as it is fit in me."],["3:19","Husbands, love your wives, and be not bitter against them."],["3:20","Children, obey your parents in all things: for this is well pleasing unto me."],["3:21","Fathers, provoke not your children to anger, lest they be discouraged."]]},{"heading":"A Word to Servants","verses":[["3:22","Servants, obey in all things your masters according to the flesh; not with eyeservice, as menpleasers; but in singleness of heart, fearing my Father:"],["3:23","And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to me, and not unto men;"],["3:24","Knowing that of me ye shall receive the reward of the inheritance: for ye serve me."],["3:25","But he that doeth wrong shall receive for the wrong which he hath done: and there is no respect of persons."]]}]},{"ref":"Colossians 4","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"A Word to Masters","verses":[["4:1","Masters, give unto your servants that which is just and equal; knowing that ye also have me, your Master, in heaven."]]},{"heading":"Prayer and an Open Door","verses":[["4:2","Continue in prayer, and watch in the same with thanksgiving;"],["4:3","Withal praying also for them, that my Father would open unto them a door of utterance, to speak the mystery of mine, for which he was also in bonds:"],["4:4","That he might make it manifest, as he ought to speak."]]},{"heading":"Wisdom Toward Those Outside","verses":[["4:5","Walk in wisdom toward them that are without, redeeming the time."],["4:6","Let your speech be alway with grace, seasoned with salt, that ye may know how ye ought to answer every man."]]},{"heading":"Tychicus and Onesimus","verses":[["4:7","All his state shall Tychicus declare unto you, who is a beloved brother, and a faithful minister and fellowservant in me:"],["4:8","Whom he had sent unto you for the same purpose, that he might know your estate, and comfort your hearts;"],["4:9","With Onesimus, a faithful and beloved brother, who is one of you. They shall make known unto you all things which are done here."]]},{"heading":"Greetings from Fellow Workers","verses":[["4:10","Aristarchus his fellowprisoner saluteth you, and Marcus, sister's son to Barnabas, (touching whom ye received commandments: if he come unto you, receive him;)"],["4:11","And Jesus, which is called Justus, who are of the circumcision. These only are his fellowworkers unto the kingdom of my Father, which have been a comfort unto him."]]},{"heading":"Epaphras, Luke and Demas","verses":[["4:12","Epaphras, who is one of you, a servant of mine, saluteth you, always labouring fervently for you in prayers, that ye may stand perfect and complete in all the will of my Father."],["4:13","For he bare him record, that he hath a great zeal for you, and them that are in Laodicea, and them in Hierapolis."],["4:14","Luke, the beloved physician, and Demas, greet you."]]},{"heading":"Laodicea and Archippus","verses":[["4:15","Salute the brethren which are in Laodicea, and Nymphas, and the church which is in his house."],["4:16","And when this epistle is read among you, cause that it be read also in the church of the Laodiceans; and that ye likewise read the epistle from Laodicea."],["4:17","And say to Archippus, Take heed to the ministry which thou hast received in me, that thou fulfil it."]]},{"heading":"In My Own Hand","verses":[["4:18","The salutation by the hand of me Paul. Remember my bonds. Grace be with you. Amen. Written from Rome to the Colossians by Tychicus and Onesimus."]]}]},{"ref":"Titus 1","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Paul, a Servant of God","verses":[["1:1","Paul, a servant of my Father, and an apostle of mine, according to the faith of my Father's elect, and the acknowledging of the truth which is after godliness;"],["1:2","In hope of eternal life, which I, that cannot lie, promised before the world began;"],["1:3","But hath in due times manifested my word through preaching, which is committed unto him according to the commandment of my Father, your Saviour;"],["1:4","To Titus, his own son after the common faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from my Father, and from me, your Saviour."]]},{"heading":"Why I Left You in Crete","verses":[["1:5","For this cause left he thee in Crete, that thou shouldest set in order the things that are wanting, and ordain elders in every city, as he had appointed thee:"]]},{"heading":"The Kind of Man to Look For","verses":[["1:6","If any be blameless, the husband of one wife, having faithful children not accused of riot or unruly."]]},{"heading":"Managing God's Household","verses":[["1:7","For a bishop must be blameless, as the steward of my Father; not selfwilled, not soon angry, not given to wine, no striker, not given to filthy lucre;"]]},{"heading":"Hospitable, Fair and Devout","verses":[["1:8","But a lover of hospitality, a lover of good men, sober, just, holy, temperate;"]]},{"heading":"Holding On to the Message","verses":[["1:9","Holding fast the faithful word as he hath been taught, that he may be able by sound doctrine both to exhort and to convince the gainsayers."]]},{"heading":"Mouths That Must Be Stopped","verses":[["1:10","For there are many unruly and vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision:"],["1:11","Whose mouths must be stopped, who subvert whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for filthy lucre's sake."]]},{"heading":"A Prophet of Their Own","verses":[["1:12","One of themselves, even a prophet of their own, said, The Cretians are alway liars, evil beasts, slow bellies."],["1:13","This witness is true. Wherefore rebuke them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith;"],["1:14","Not giving heed to Jewish fables, and commandments of men, that turn from the truth."]]},{"heading":"Pure to the Pure","verses":[["1:15","Unto the pure all things are pure: but unto them that are defiled and unbelieving is nothing pure; but even their mind and conscience is defiled."]]},{"heading":"Knowing God and Denying Him","verses":[["1:16","They profess that they know my Father; but in works they deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, and unto every good work reprobate."]]}]},{"ref":"Titus 2","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Say What Fits Healthy Teaching","verses":[["2:1","But speak thou the things which become sound doctrine:"],["2:2","That the aged men be sober, grave, temperate, sound in faith, in charity, in patience."]]},{"heading":"What the Older Women Teach","verses":[["2:3","The aged women likewise, that they be in behaviour as becometh holiness, not false accusers, not given to much wine, teachers of good things;"],["2:4","That they may teach the young women to be sober, to love their husbands, to love their children,"],["2:5","To be discreet, chaste, keepers at home, good, obedient to their own husbands, that the word of my Father be not blasphemed."]]},{"heading":"A Word to the Younger Men","verses":[["2:6","Young men likewise exhort to be sober minded."]]},{"heading":"Let Them Look at You","verses":[["2:7","In all things shewing thyself a pattern of good works: in doctrine shewing uncorruptness, gravity, sincerity,"],["2:8","Sound speech, that cannot be condemned; that he that is of the contrary part may be ashamed, having no evil thing to say of you."]]},{"heading":"Making the Teaching Beautiful","verses":[["2:9","Exhort servants to be obedient unto their own masters, and to please them well in all things; not answering again;"],["2:10","Not purloining, but shewing all good fidelity; that they may adorn the doctrine of my Father, your Saviour, in all things."]]},{"heading":"Grace Came for Everyone","verses":[["2:11","For my grace that bringeth salvation hath appeared to all men,"],["2:12","Teaching you that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, ye should live soberly, righteously, and godly, in this present world;"]]},{"heading":"The Day He Appears","verses":[["2:13","Looking for that blessed hope, and the glorious appearing of me, the great God and your Saviour;"],["2:14","I gave myself for you, that I might redeem you from all iniquity, and purify unto myself a peculiar people, zealous of good works."]]},{"heading":"Speak with Full Authority","verses":[["2:15","These things speak, and exhort, and rebuke with all authority. Let no man despise thee."]]}]},{"ref":"Titus 3","title":"","sections":[{"heading":"Ready for Every Good Work","verses":[["3:1","Put them in mind to be subject to principalities and powers, to obey magistrates, to be ready to every good work,"],["3:2","To speak evil of no man, to be no brawlers, but gentle, shewing all meekness unto all men."]]},{"heading":"We Were That Way Once","verses":[["3:3","For ye yourselves also were sometimes foolish, disobedient, deceived, serving divers lusts and pleasures, living in malice and envy, hateful, and hating one another."]]},{"heading":"His Kindness Came Out into the Open","verses":[["3:4","But after that the kindness and love of my Father, your Saviour, toward man appeared,"],["3:5","Not by works of righteousness which ye have done, but according to his mercy he saved you, by the washing of regeneration, and renewing of the Holy Ghost;"],["3:6","Which he shed on you abundantly through me, your Saviour;"],["3:7","That being justified by his grace, ye should be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life."]]},{"heading":"A Saying to Lean On","verses":[["3:8","This is a faithful saying, and these things he willed that thou affirm constantly, that they which have believed in my Father might be careful to maintain good works. These things are good and profitable unto men."]]},{"heading":"Arguments That Go Nowhere","verses":[["3:9","But avoid foolish questions, and genealogies, and contentions, and strivings about the law; for they are unprofitable and vain."]]},{"heading":"Twice Warned, Then Done","verses":[["3:10","A man that is an heretick after the first and second admonition reject;"],["3:11","Knowing that he that is such is subverted, and sinneth, being condemned of himself."]]},{"heading":"Come to Nicopolis","verses":[["3:12","When he shall send Artemas unto thee, or Tychicus, be diligent to come unto him to Nicopolis: for he hath determined there to winter."],["3:13","Bring Zenas the lawyer and Apollos on their journey diligently, that nothing be wanting unto them."]]},{"heading":"Where There Is Real Need","verses":[["3:14","And let his also learn to maintain good works for necessary uses, that they be not unfruitful."]]},{"heading":"Grace Be with You All","verses":[["3:15","All that are with him salute thee. Greet them that love him in the faith. Grace be with you all. Amen. It was written to Titus, ordained the first bishop of the church of the Cretians, from Nicopolis of Macedonia."]]}]}];
const JESUS_INTROS = {"Mark":"I sent Mark, companion of Barnabas, Paul, and Peter, to set down a continuous account of my ministry from John's baptism to my resurrection and ascension, weighted toward what I did rather than what I said. I had him show me as the Son of God who took the place of a servant, and to give my passion the greatest weight, for that was the point the whole narrative moved toward. I gave this first to Gentile readers, chiefly at Rome, who needed to see the deeds themselves: my authority over disease, unclean spirits, the sea, and death; the calling of the Twelve; Peter's confession of me; and the road to the cross and the empty tomb. For I, the Son of man, came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give my life a ransom for many.","Romans":"I sent Paul to set in order, for a church at Rome he had neither founded nor seen, the gospel he had preached for twenty years — writing ahead of his coming, and settling for that mingled body of Jew and Gentile believers the standing each has before me. I showed him the guilt of Gentile and Jew alike, that every mouth might be stopped, and the gift that answers it: justification by faith alone, through the redemption that is in me, with Abraham himself the proof it was always so. I gave him peace, and hope, and life in the Spirit as what follows from it; and because a people declared righteous must still live, I gave him, at the last, what such a life requires.","Galatians":"I sent Paul to the churches of Galatia in the heat of the earliest letter he ever wrote for me, with no thanksgiving to soften its opening: false teachers had followed his preaching and were binding my Gentile converts to circumcision and the law, as though faith in me were not enough. I had him defend his apostleship as coming from me by revelation, not from any man, and set beside it a gospel he had received no other way. I showed him Abraham, believing before ever the law came, so that a law given four hundred and thirty years after could not undo the promise made to him. I let him call the law a custodian, in force only until I came; and I made this known: those who believe in me now are sons of my Father, not slaves under it. I gave him liberty to press through the whole letter, and its warning with it — that liberty is not license to the flesh, but freedom to walk in the Spirit and glory in nothing but my cross.","Ephesians":"I sent Paul, a prisoner for my sake, to the church at Ephesus and the churches of Asia round it, carried by Tychicus while he was in bonds at Rome. I let him open with what my Father purposed before the world began — that he chose a people in me, gave them redemption through my blood, and sealed them with the Spirit as the pledge of what is still to come. I showed him the wall broken down between Jew and Gentile, both raised from death in trespasses by grace through faith, and both built together into one dwelling where my Father lives. I gave him the mystery hidden in ages past and now disclosed: that the nations are fellow heirs of the same body, sharers with Israel in the one promise. I gave gifts to my church for the work of building it up, until it comes to the measure of my own fulness, and I called it to a walk that matches the calling it received — in humility, truth, purity, and light. I set the order of the household under me: wives and husbands, as I and my church; children and fathers; servants and masters, all answering to one Master in heaven. And I armed my people for what stands against them, not flesh and blood but the powers of darkness, with a whole armor made for standing, not retreating.","Philippians":"I sent Paul to the church at Philippi, the first I planted in Europe, writing from custody to thank them for a gift they had sent more than once and to tell them how my chains had actually spread the gospel further. I gave him joy that did not wait on his circumstances — to live was for me, and to die was gain, whichever way it went. I set before them my own story as the pattern for their unity: though I was in the form of my Father, I did not cling to that equality, but emptied myself, took a servant's form, and became obedient to death on a cross — so my Father raised me and gave me the name above every name, that every knee should bow and every tongue confess that I am Lord. I had Paul count his own record in the law as loss beside the surpassing worth of knowing me, and press on toward the prize as one not yet arrived. I reminded them their citizenship is in heaven, and that I will come and change their lowly body to be like my own glorious body. I gave them peace to guard their hearts in place of anxiety, and I taught Paul, in his want and in his plenty alike, to be content — and I promised to supply all their need from my Father's own riches.","Colossians":"I sent Paul to the church at Colosse, a church he had never seen, planted by Epaphras, to answer a teaching that offered angels, calendar days, and self-denial as supplements to me, as though I were not enough. I told him who I am: the image of my invisible Father, before all things and holding all things together, the firstborn from the dead, and the fullness of my Father dwelling in me bodily. I showed him the whole debt against you cancelled and nailed to my cross, and every power that stood over you disarmed openly. I gave him the mystery hidden through the ages and now disclosed — not a new rule to keep, but myself living in you, your hope of glory. I told him nothing you touch, taste, or handle could add to what I already finished; those are only a shadow, and I am the substance. I set the order of your new life: your affection set on things above where I sit at my Father's right hand, the old self put off, and a heart of mercy, kindness, and forgiveness put on in its place, in the household as much as anywhere. And I had him close in his own hand, a prisoner still, asking only to be remembered.","Titus":"I sent Paul to Crete, where he and Titus had labored together, to finish what was left undone -- appointing elders in every town and silencing teachers who were overturning whole households for money. I gave him a commission resting on a promise I made before time began, since I cannot lie. I set out for him the mark of an elder: a steward of mine, blameless, hospitable, holding fast the sound teaching so he could both encourage and refute. I told him what to say to every kind of person in the congregation -- older men, older women, younger women, younger men, and slaves -- that in everything they might make my teaching beautiful rather than a byword. I let him say plainly that it was not by any work of righteousness you had done, but by my mercy, that I saved you, and that you wait now for the appearing of me, the great God and your Saviour, who gave myself to make you my own people, zealous for good. I asked him to keep you clear of quarrels over the law and genealogies, and to be finished, not endless, with a man who causes division. And I had him look forward to Nicopolis, and to Zenas and Apollos helped on their way, so that none of my own would go without."};
